    <node id="Abuta">
      <data key="d0">supplement</data>
      <data key="d1">Cissampelos pareira</data>
      <data key="d2">Aaknadi | Bejunco de Cerca | Bhatindupat | Butua | False Pareira | Feuille de Velous | Herbe des Sages-Femmes | Krueo Ma Noy | Krung Kha Mao | Menispermaceae</data>
      <data key="d3">https://naturalmedicines.therapeuticresearch.com/Data/ProMonographs/Abuta</data>
      <data key="d4">Abuta is a climbing plant distributed in tropical areas of Asia, Africa, North America, and South America. It is sometimes used as medicine . It has traditionally been used for gastrointestinal disorders, menstrual disorders, and as a diuretic, aphrodisiac, antiseptic, stimulant, and sedative.</data>
      <data key="d5">⚠️ AVOID: Insufficient reliable information available; avoid using.</data>
      <data key="d6" />
