    <node id="Acetyl-L-Carnitine">
      <data key="d0">supplement</data>
      <data key="d1" />
      <data key="d2">Acetil-L-Carnitina | Acetil-L-carnitina | Acetyl Carnitine | Acetyl Carnitine | Acétyl Carnitine | Acetyl L-Carnitine | Acetyl L-Carnitine Hydrochloride | Acetyl-Carnitine | Acétyl-L-Carnitine | Acetyl-L-Carnitine Arginate Dihydrochloride</data>
      <data key="d3">https://naturalmedicines.therapeuticresearch.com/Data/ProMonographs/Acetyl-L-Carnitine</data>
      <data key="d4">Acetyl-L-carnitine is an ester of the amino acid derivative, L-carnitine. L-carnitine is naturally found in the body . Acetyl-L-carnitine is the most abundant of the L-carnitine esters in the body. L-carnitine is made in the human brain, liver, and kidneys from the amino acids lysine and methionine</data>
      <data key="d5">⚠️ AVOID: Insufficient reliable information available; avoid using.</data>
      <data key="d6" />
