    <node id="Ackee">
      <data key="d0">supplement</data>
      <data key="d1">Blighia sapida</data>
      <data key="d2">Ackée | Akee | Akée | Aki | Akí | Anjye | Arbre à Fricassée | Arbre Fricasse | Daki | Gwanja</data>
      <data key="d3">https://naturalmedicines.therapeuticresearch.com/Data/ProMonographs/Ackee</data>
      <data key="d4">Ackee refers to the fruit-bearing evergreen tree Blighia sapida. Ripe ackee fruit is eaten as food in West Africa and in the Caribbean . It is a dietary staple and the national fruit of Jamaica . Ackee is also found in southern Florida and Central America . Despite its popular use in other countries</data>
      <data key="d5">⚠️ AVOID: Unsafe when the unripe fruit is ingested . There is insufficient reliable information available about the safety of the ripe fruit during pregnancy and breast-feeding; avoid using.</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
