    <node id="Acupressure">
      <data key="d0">supplement</data>
      <data key="d1" />
      <data key="d2">Active Acupressure (synonyms: Acupoint Massage | Acupression Active | Acupression Auriculaire | Acupression Chinoise | Acupression du Pied | Acupression Occidentale | Acupression Passive | Aroma Acupressure | Aromatherapy Acupressure | Auricular Acupressure</data>
      <data key="d3">https://naturalmedicines.therapeuticresearch.com/Data/ProMonographs/Acupressure</data>
      <data key="d4">Acupressure is a common treatment modality of traditional Chinese medicine (TCM). Acupressure is similar to acupuncture, except that it involves the use of applied pressure in place of needles. Pressure is applied using hands, thumbs, fingers, or devices to specific places, or acupoints, on the body</data>
      <data key="d5">✅ SAFE: Possibly Safe when used appropriately. Acupressure has been safely used during pregnancy in clinical trials without significant adverse effects .</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
