      <data key="d2">Agrimone | Agrimonia | Aigremoine | Aigremoine Eupatoire | Church Steeples | Churchsteeples | Cockeburr | Cocklebur | Common Agrimony | Da Hua Long Ya Cao</data>
      <data key="d3">https://naturalmedicines.therapeuticresearch.com/Data/ProMonographs/Agrimony</data>
      <data key="d4">Agrimony is an herb widely distributed in the Northern hemisphere. The dried leaves and seeds have been traditionally used as medicine . Traditional uses include bleeding, diabetes, and sore throat, as well as cardiovascular, gallbladder, gastrointestinal, kidney, liver, and skin conditions.</data>
      <data key="d5">⚠️ AVOID: Possibly Unsafe when used orally due to possible effects on the menstrual cycle .</data>
