      <data key="d3">https://naturalmedicines.therapeuticresearch.com/Data/ProMonographs/Alder-Buckthorn</data>
      <data key="d4">Alder buckthorn is a type of invasive shrub. It is native to bright wetlands in Europe but also grows in North America . The bark is traditionally used as medicine. However, chronic use is associated with damage to gastrointestinal epithelial cells, pigmentation of the colonic mucosa, known as pseud</data>
      <data key="d5">ℹ️ No pregnancy data available. Consult your physician.</data>
