    <node id="Algal Oil">
      <data key="d0">supplement</data>
      <data key="d1" />
      <data key="d2">Aceite de Algas | DHA-S Oil | DHASCO Oil | DHASCO-S | DHASCO-T | DHA-T Oil | High DHA Algal Triacylglycerol | High EPA Algal Oil | High-Oleic Algal Oil | Huile algale</data>
      <data key="d3">https://naturalmedicines.therapeuticresearch.com/Data/ProMonographs/Algal-Oil</data>
      <data key="d4">Algal oil is a type of oil derived from marine algae such as Crypthecodinium, Nannochloropsis, Schizochytrium, Prototheca, or Ulkenia species . These algae are preferentially cultivated using algaculture to produce algal oils rich in specific fatty acids, including oleic acid, docosahexaenoic acid (</data>
      <data key="d5">✅ SAFE: Likely Safe when used orally and appropriately. Docosahexaenoic acid (DHA)-enriched algal oil is commonly included as a component of prenatal vitamins. Algal oil providing DHA 400-600 mg daily during pregnancy has been used with apparent safety in most clinical research . When taken as a prenatal supplement, DHA-enriched algal oil increases DHA levels in breast milk . Taking DHA-enriched algal oil during lactation also increases levels of DHA in breast milk . One study found that using DHA-enric</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
