    <node id="Chromium">
      <data key="d0">supplement</data>
      <data key="d1" />
      <data key="d2">Acétate de Chrome | Chélate de Chrome | Chelated Chromium | Chlorure Chromique | Chlorure de Chrome | Chrome | Chrome 3+ | Chrome Chélaté | Chrome Facteur de Tolérance au Glucose | Chrome FTG</data>
      <data key="d3">https://naturalmedicines.therapeuticresearch.com/Data/ProMonographs/Chromium</data>
      <data key="d4">Chromium is a trace mineral. It exists in two forms: trivalent and hexavalent states. Trivalent chromium (Cr III), the form found in foods and supplements, is biologically active and safe . The other form of chromium, hexavalent chromium (Cr VI), is a known toxin that can cause skin problems and lun</data>
      <data key="d5">✅ SAFE: Likely Safe when used orally and appropriately in amounts not exceeding adequate intake (AI) levels. The AI for pregnancy is 28 mcg daily for those 14-18 years of age and 30 mcg daily for those 19-50 years of age .</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Copper">
      <data key="d0">supplement</data>
      <data key="d1">Atomic number</data>
      <data key="d2">Chélate de Cuivre | Chelated Copper | Citrate de Cuivre | Cobre | Cobre Quelado | Copper Ascorbate | Copper Chelate | Copper Citrate | Copper Gluconate | Copper Sulfate</data>
      <data key="d3">https://naturalmedicines.therapeuticresearch.com/Data/ProMonographs/Copper</data>
      <data key="d4">Copper is an essential trace mineral found in foods such as organ meats and seafood, nuts and seeds, grain and cocoa products, and water, especially water from copper pipes . Copper was historically used for preventing infections during burn healing . CHILDREN: Likely Safe when used orally and appro</data>
      <data key="d5">⚠️ AVOID: Likely Safe when used orally and appropriately. Copper is safe in amounts that do not exceed the tolerable upper intake level (UL) of 8 mg daily for those 14-18 years of age or 10 mg daily for those 19 years and older .</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Strontium">
      <data key="d0">supplement</data>
      <data key="d1" />
      <data key="d2">Chlorure de Strontium | Chlorure de Strontium-89 | Citrate de Strontium | Estroncio | Gluconate de Strontium | Numéro Atomique 38 | Ranélate de Strontium | Stable Strontium | Strontium Chloride | Strontium Citrate</data>
      <data key="d3">https://naturalmedicines.therapeuticresearch.com/Data/ProMonographs/Strontium</data>
      <data key="d4">Strontium is an element found in the human body and nature . It has four known stable forms and 12 known radioactive isotopes . In the human body, more than 99% of strontium is stored in the bone and teeth. Strontium is physically and chemically similar to calcium, readily substitutes for calcium, a</data>
      <data key="d5">✅ SAFE: Likely Safe when consumed orally in food amounts. Strontium has not been linked to toxicity when consumed in dietary amounts, which are typically about 0.5 mg to 1.5 mg/day . ...when strontium chloride is used topically and appropriately as a toothpaste . Strontium chloride hexahydrate (Sensodyne-SC) is an FDA approved product.</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Alkaline Diet">
      <data key="d0">supplement</data>
      <data key="d1" />
      <data key="d2">Acid Ash Diet | Acid-Alkaline Diet | Alkaline Acid Diet | Alkaline Ash Diet | Dieta Alcalina | pH Diet | Régime alcalin</data>
      <data key="d3">https://naturalmedicines.therapeuticresearch.com/Data/ProMonographs/Alkaline-Diet</data>
      <data key="d4">The alkaline diet is based on the idea that a person should consume foods that are slightly alkaline. Advocates claim that consuming a diet high in acidic foods may disrupt the pH of the bloodstream and increase the likelihood of chronic or degenerative diseases. Scientific research has not evaluate</data>
      <data key="d5">⚠️ AVOID: Insufficient reliable information available; avoid using unless under medical advisement.</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
