      <data key="d3">https://naturalmedicines.therapeuticresearch.com/Data/ProMonographs/Alkanna</data>
      <data key="d4">Alkanna is a plant that grows in many parts of Europe, the Mediterranean, and Western Asia. The roots and leaves are used in medicine. The roots are also used as a coloring agent in the pharmaceutical, cosmetic, fabric, food, and liquor industries . However, some alkanna products contain hepatotoxic</data>
