      <data key="d1">Aluminum phosphate</data>
      <data key="d2">Anhydrous Sodium Phosphate | Bone Phosphate | Calcium Orthophosphate | Calcium Phosphate Dibasic Anhydrous | Calcium Phosphate Dibasic Dihydrate | Calcium Phosphate Dibasique Anhydre | Calcium Phosphate Dibasique Dihydrate | Calcium Phosphate Tribasic | Calcium Phosphate Tribasique | Calcium Phosphate-Bone Ash</data>
      <data key="d3">https://naturalmedicines.therapeuticresearch.com/Data/ProMonographs/Phosphate-Salts</data>
      <data key="d4">Phosphorus is an essential mineral. In the diet, the best sources of phosphorus are animal foods high in protein such as meat, fish, eggs, and dairy products . In the diet and body, phosphorus is usually bound to other minerals in the form of a phosphate salt. Phosphate salts are not the same as org</data>
      <data key="d5">✅ SAFE: Likely Safe when used orally and appropriately at the recommended dietary allowance (RDA) of 1250 mg daily for individuals 14-18 years of age and 700 mg daily for those over 18 years of age . ...when sodium phosphate is used rectally and appropriately short-term . ...when used intravenously. Intravenous potassium phosphate is an FDA-approved prescription drug .</data>
