      <data key="d4">American elder is a plant. The flower and ripe berry are used in traditional medicine. The fruit is also used as a flavoring component in foods and beverages. The stem contains cyanogenic glycosides and has been reported to cause toxicity in children .</data>
      <data key="d5">⚠️ AVOID: Likely Unsafe when the leaves, stems, or unripe fruit are used orally . There is insufficient reliable information available about the safety of the flower or cooked fruit during pregnancy or lactation; avoid using.</data>
