      <data key="d3">https://naturalmedicines.therapeuticresearch.com/Data/ProMonographs/American-Hellebore</data>
      <data key="d4">American hellebore is a poisonous and cardiotoxic plant . It is native to the swampy areas and low woodlands of the eastern and western United States and Canada. It can grow to 8 feet tall and has large pleated leaves and yellow, pink, or white flowers. As the plant is maturing, it may be mistaken f</data>
      <data key="d5">⚠️ AVOID: Likely Unsafe when used orally or topically. Alkaloids American hellebore are considered toxic ; avoid using.</data>
