      <data key="d4">American ivy is a climbing shrub native to North America and cultivated worldwide. The bark is used in medicine . KEY HIGHLIGHTS - Sometimes used for digestive disorders, to stimulate sweating, and for other conditions, but there is no strong evidence to support any use. - Insufficient reliable info</data>
