      <data key="d2">4-Androstene 3 | 17-dione | 4-Androstenedione | Andro | Androstene | Androstenediona | Androsténédione | Androstènedione</data>
      <data key="d3">https://naturalmedicines.therapeuticresearch.com/Data/ProMonographs/Androstenedione</data>
      <data key="d4">Androstenedione is a precursor to testosterone, estrogen, and other androgens. It is naturally produced in the body in the adrenal glands and gonads. In men, most androstenedione comes from the testes . In March 2004, the US Food and Drug Administration (FDA) told manufacturers of dietary supplement</data>
      <data key="d5">⚠️ AVOID: Likely Unsafe when used orally. Androstenedione might induce labor .</data>
      <data key="d6" />
