      <data key="d4">Angelica archangelica is a perennial herb that grows to 50-250 cm in height and has a thick stem and very large leaves. It is native to the coasts of the North and Baltic Seas, growing as far north as Lapland and also in Iceland . It is used in cooking, as a medicine, and as a flavoring agent in bev</data>
