      <data key="d4">Anhydrous crystalline maltose is a disaccharide composed of two D-glucose molecules connected by an alpha (1→4) bond . It is produced by enzymatic degradation of starch . It has been used as a food stabilizer, and also as a desiccant in foods, cosmetics, and pharmaceuticals .</data>
