      <data key="d4">Antineoplastons are a group of peptide fractions that were observed to be absent in the urine of cancer patients by Stanislaw Burzynski, MD, PhD, in the late 1970s . As these compounds were found in the blood and urine of healthy individuals, it was hypothesized that these substances may have antitu</data>
