      <data key="d4">Ayahuasca is a psychotropic drink that is used for therapeutic and religious ritual purposes in several Amazonian countries, including Brazil, Peru, Colombia, and Ecuador. The word "ayahuasca" comes from the words, aya, meaning spirit or soul, and huasca, meaning rope or vine, in the Quechua languag</data>
      <data key="d5">⚠️ AVOID: Likely Unsafe when used orally. In addition to its hallucinogenic effects, animal research shows that chronic administration of higher doses of ayahuasca to pregnant animals causes toxicity in the offspring . Avoid using.</data>
