      <data key="d4">Bacillus coagulans is a spore-forming, lactic acid-producing, gram-positive bacterium . Bacillus coagulans has recently been reclassified as Weizmannia coagulans . Despite this update, most commercial products continue to use the name B. coagulans, and others use a further outdated classification, L</data>
