      <data key="d3">https://naturalmedicines.therapeuticresearch.com/Data/ProMonographs/Bacillus-subtilis</data>
      <data key="d4">Bacillus subtilis is an aerobic or facultative-anaerobic, spore-forming, gram-positive bacteria. It commonly inhabits the gastrointestinal tract and is used as a probiotic . It is used to ferment soy to make food such as natto . Some commercial products marketed as B. subtilis instead contain newly</data>
