      <data key="d3">https://naturalmedicines.therapeuticresearch.com/Data/ProMonographs/Belladonna</data>
      <data key="d4">Belladonna is a perennial, herbaceous plant that grows from Western Europe to the Himalayas, and is also cultivated in the US . All parts of the plant are poisonous . The name "belladonna" (beautiful lady) refers to its historical, cosmetic use to dilate pupils, which was considered to increase beau</data>
      <data key="d5">⚠️ AVOID: Likely Unsafe when used orally. Belladonna contains toxic alkaloids and has been linked to reports of serious adverse effects .</data>
