      <data key="d3">https://naturalmedicines.therapeuticresearch.com/Data/ProMonographs/Beta-Glucans</data>
      <data key="d4">Beta-glucans are soluble fibers derived from the cell walls of algae, bacteria, and fungi, and from plants such as oat and barley . The US Food and Drug Administration (FDA) allows food products containing at least 750 mg of beta-glucans per serving to be labeled with a health claim stating that it</data>
      <data key="d5">⚠️ AVOID: Insufficient reliable information available; avoid using.</data>
