      <data key="d3">https://naturalmedicines.therapeuticresearch.com/Data/ProMonographs/Betaine-Anhydrous</data>
      <data key="d4">Betaine anhydrous is a chemical that occurs naturally in the body. It is produced by oxidation of choline in the liver and kidneys . Betaine anhydrous is also found in foods such as beets, spinach, whole grains, liver, eggs, and seafood . CHILDREN: Likely Safe when used orally and appropriately in d</data>
