      <data key="d2">Acide Chlorhydrique de Bétaïne | Betaine Chlorhydrate | Betaine HCl | Bétaïne HCl | Betaine Hydrochloric Acid | Chlorhidrato de Betaína | Chlorhydrate de Bétaïne | Chlorhydrate de bétaïne | Chlorhydrate de Triméthylglycine | Clorhidrato de betaína</data>
      <data key="d3">https://naturalmedicines.therapeuticresearch.com/Data/ProMonographs/Betaine-Hydrochloride</data>
      <data key="d4">Betaine, which is produced by oxidation of choline, occurs naturally in the body. It is a methyl derivative of the amino acid glycine . Betaine hydrochloride is a salt form of betaine that was previously marketed over-the-counter (OTC) as a source of hydrochloric acid for people with low stomach aci</data>
