      <data key="d2">ß-Me-PEA | ß-Methylphenethylamine | 1-Amino-2-Phenylpropane | 1-Phenyl-1-Methyl-2-Aminoethane | 2-Aminoisopropylbenzene | 2-Phenyl-1-Propanamin | 2-Phenyl-1-Propanamine | 2-Phenylpropylamine | Alpha-Benzylethylamine | Beta-Me-PEA</data>
      <data key="d3">https://naturalmedicines.therapeuticresearch.com/Data/ProMonographs/BetaMethylphenethylamine-BMPEA</data>
      <data key="d4">Beta-methylphenethylamine (BMPEA) is a stimulant and positional isomer of amphetamine that was first synthesized in the 1930s as a replacement for amphetamine. It is found in some commercially available dietary supplements. In many cases, it is labelled as being sourced from Acacia rigidula, althoug</data>
      <data key="d5">⚠️ AVOID: Possibly Unsafe when used orally. BMPEA is an amphetamine-like compound that has been shown to have stimulant properties and is associated with severe cardiovascular adverse effects .</data>
      <data key="d6" />
