      <data key="d4">Bifidobacteria are a type of lactic acid- and acetic acid-producing bacteria that are natural inhabitants of the human gastrointestinal tract . B. breve is commonly found in the gastrointestinal tract of breastfed infants and also in the vagina . B. breve and other bifidobacteria are included in pro</data>
      <data key="d5">✅ SAFE: Possibly Safe when used orally and appropriately. In clinical research, Bifidobacterium breve has been used safely beginning from 16 weeks gestation and continued into the postpartum period .</data>
      <data key="d6" />
