      <data key="d3">https://naturalmedicines.therapeuticresearch.com/Data/ProMonographs/Vitamin-B12</data>
      <data key="d4">Vitamin B12 is an essential water-soluble vitamin that is commonly found in a variety of foods, such as fish, shellfish, meat, eggs, and dairy products . It is frequently used in combination with other B vitamins in vitamin B complex formulations. Methylcobalamin is the active form of vitamin B12. C</data>
      <data key="d5">⚠️ AVOID: Likely Safe when used orally in amounts that do not exceed the recommended dietary allowance (RDA). The RDA for vitamin B12 during pregnancy is 2.6 mcg daily . There is insufficient reliable information available about the safety of larger amounts of vitamin B12 during pregnancy.</data>
