      <data key="d3">https://naturalmedicines.therapeuticresearch.com/Data/ProMonographs/Bitter-Almond</data>
      <data key="d4">Bitter almond is a variety of almond. Bitter almond oil contains a toxic compound called amygdalin, which produces hydrocyanic acid and benzaldehyde . Products referred to as "bitter almond" volatile oils can also be produced from other related fruit kernels including apricot, peach, and plum. Simil</data>
