      <data key="d3">https://naturalmedicines.therapeuticresearch.com/Data/ProMonographs/Bitter-Melon</data>
      <data key="d4">Bitter melon is an annual climbing vine that grows in India, Asia, East Africa, South America, and the Caribbean. It is used as a vegetable in India and other Asian countries, sometimes as an ingredient in curries. It has also been used traditionally in these countries for the treatment of diabetes</data>
      <data key="d5">⚠️ AVOID: Possibly Unsafe when used orally. Animal research shows that two proteins isolated from the raw fruit of bitter melon possess abortifacient properties . Also, one animal study shows that bitter melon juice significantly reduces the fertility rate of mice . However, these effects of bitter melon have not been assessed in humans.</data>
