      <data key="d4">Camellia sinensis is a woody plant . The dried leaves and leaf buds are used to produce various types of teas, including black tea, green tea, and oolong tea . Black tea, the most commonly consumed tea, and oolong tea involve processes in which the leaves are fermented (black tea) or partially ferme</data>
