    <node id="Boldo">
      <data key="d0">supplement</data>
      <data key="d1">Peumus boldus</data>
      <data key="d2">Boldine | Boldo Folium | Boldoak Boldea | Boldus | Boldus Boldus | Peumus boldus Molina</data>
      <data key="d3">https://naturalmedicines.therapeuticresearch.com/Data/ProMonographs/Boldo</data>
      <data key="d4">Boldo is a tree or evergreen shrub native to the Andean region of South America. It is most commonly found in Chile . It has been traditionally used as a diuretic, sedative, antiseptic, and antispasmodic .</data>
      <data key="d5">⚠️ AVOID: Possibly Unsafe when used orally in medicinal amounts. In animals, boldo and the constituent boldine have abortive and teratogenic effects . Also, the ascaridole constituent of boldo is a liver toxin .</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
