    <node id="Boron">
      <data key="d0">supplement</data>
      <data key="d1">Atomic number</data>
      <data key="d2">Acide Borique | Anhydride Borique | B (symbole chimique) | Borate | Borate de Sodium | Borates | Bore | Bore Chélaté | Boric Acid | Boric Anhydride</data>
      <data key="d3">https://naturalmedicines.therapeuticresearch.com/Data/ProMonographs/Boron</data>
      <data key="d4">Boron is an element found in water and in foods such as nuts and vegetables, often as part of natural compounds such as calcium fructoborate. Boric acid is used as an astringent, to prevent skin infection, and as an ophthalmic irrigant . Historically, both the Babylonians and Egyptians are thought t</data>
      <data key="d5">⚠️ AVOID: Likely Safe when used orally and appropriately. Boron is safe in amounts that do not exceed the UL during pregnancy or lactation, which is 20 mg daily in those 19-50 years of age or 17 mg daily for those 14-18 years of age .</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
