    <node id="Broccoli">
      <data key="d0">supplement</data>
      <data key="d1">Brassica oleracea</data>
      <data key="d2">Brassica Oleracea Italica Group | Broccoli Flower | Brocoli | Brócoli | Calabrese | Purple Sprouting Broccoli</data>
      <data key="d3">https://naturalmedicines.therapeuticresearch.com/Data/ProMonographs/Broccoli</data>
      <data key="d4">Broccoli, a common vegetable, is one of several crop varieties of the Brassica oleracea species. Other varieties of this species include kale, cabbage, Brussels sprout, and cauliflower .</data>
      <data key="d5">⚠️ AVOID: Likely Safe when used orally in food amounts . There is insufficient reliable information available about the safety of broccoli when used in medicinal amounts during pregnancy and lactation; avoid using.</data>
