      <data key="d3">https://naturalmedicines.therapeuticresearch.com/Data/ProMonographs/Brown-Rice</data>
      <data key="d4">Brown rice is the dehusked seed of the rice plant. It retains the bran, germ, and endosperm, unlike white rice which is milled ("polished") to remove the husk, bran, and germ, leaving only the endosperm . Brown rice can be softened by pre-germination, which allows it to germinate for 72 hours before</data>
      <data key="d5">✅ SAFE: Likely Safe when used orally in amounts commonly found in foods . There is insufficient reliable information available about the safety of brown rice when used in medicinal amounts during pregnancy or lactation.</data>
      <data key="d6" />
