      <data key="d4">The term "buchu" was traditionally used by the Khoi-San to describe any aromatic plant from the Cape area of South Africa. Today the name buchu generally refers to the species Agathosma betulina and Agathosma crenulata. Agathosma betulina is sometimes called "round-leaf buchu" while Agathosma crenul</data>
