      <data key="d4">Bulbine natalensis is a succulent plant that grows in the northern and eastern parts of South Africa . Analysis of Bulbine natalensis root obtained from open street markets in South Africa shows that the plant root might be contaminated with high levels of aluminum (5559 mg/kg dry weight) and iron (</data>
      <data key="d5">⚠️ AVOID: Possibly Unsafe when used orally in large amounts. Animal research shows that Bulbine natalensis stem extract might be embryotoxic when administered at a dose of 100 mg/kg . Until more is known about its effects in humans, avoid using during pregnancy. There is insufficient reliable information about the safety of using topical Bulbine natalensis during pregnancy; avoid using.</data>
