      <data key="d2">All-Trans Lycopène | Cis-Lycopène | Licopeno | Lycopène | Lycopenes | Lycopènes | Psi-Psi-Carotène</data>
      <data key="d3">https://naturalmedicines.therapeuticresearch.com/Data/ProMonographs/Lycopene</data>
      <data key="d4">Lycopene is a fat-soluble carotenoid similar to beta-carotene, but without provitamin A activity . It is found in tomatoes, guava, pink grapefruit, red oranges, apricots, rose hip, and watermelon. In the US, over 80% of dietary lycopene comes from tomato products .</data>
      <data key="d5">✅ SAFE: Likely Safe when consumed in amounts commonly found in foods. There is insufficient reliable information available about the safety of lycopene supplements during pregnancy. Small, low-quality clinical studies have shown conflicting results about the safety of using lycopene 2-4 mg daily during pregnancy .</data>
