      <data key="d4">Calendula is a flowering plant commonly known as marigold . It is native to Asia and southern Europe and has been traditionally used in Ayurvedic and Unani systems of medicine for topical ailments, and as an antispasmodic, antipyretic, and emmenagogue. It was also commonly used as a food dye and fla</data>
      <data key="d5">⚠️ AVOID: Likely Unsafe when used orally; contraindicated due to spermatocide, antiblastocyst, and abortifacient effects. There is insufficient reliable information available about the safety of calendula when used topically during pregnancy .</data>
