      <data key="d4">Casein protein, which gives milk its white color, is the major protein source found in milk. Dairy milk consists of around 80% casein protein and 20% whey protein . Casein protein is considered a complete protein, meaning it contains all of the essential amino acids, including the branched chain ami</data>
