      <data key="d4">Cashew is an evergreen tropical tree native to Brazil and other areas of Central and South America. It now grows in southeast Asia and Africa. Cashew nuts are commonly eaten as food. Although most tree nuts are included in the U.S. Food and Drug Administration (FDA) authorized health claim related t</data>
