      <data key="d3">https://naturalmedicines.therapeuticresearch.com/Data/ProMonographs/Cassia-Cinnamon</data>
      <data key="d4">Cassia cinnamon is a type of cinnamon prepared from the dried inner bark of an evergreen tree that grows in areas of southeastern Asia . It is the most common type of cinnamon sold in North America for use as a spice and flavoring agent . It has been used in Chinese medicine for thousands of years .</data>
      <data key="d5">✅ SAFE: Likely Safe when consumed in amounts commonly found in foods . There is insufficient reliable information available about the safety of cassia cinnamon when used in medicinal amounts during pregnancy and breast-feeding. Stay on the safe side and stick to food amounts.</data>
