      <data key="d4">Cassia nomame is an annual or short-lived leguminous plant that grows to about 1.5 meters in height. It is found in South Africa and Eastern Asia, including Korea, Japan, and China . The plant is used in foods, particularly teas . It is also marketed as an ingredient in weight-loss formulations .</data>
