    </node>
    <node id="Catechu">
      <data key="d0">supplement</data>
      <data key="d1">Black catechu</data>
      <data key="d2">Acacia catechu (synonyms: Acacia à Cachou | Acacia Cashoo | Acacia Catechu Heartwood Extract | Black Catechu | Black Cutch | Cachou | Cachou | Cachou de Pegu | Cachou Noir | Cashou</data>
      <data key="d3">https://naturalmedicines.therapeuticresearch.com/Data/ProMonographs/Catechu</data>
      <data key="d4">Catechu is a plant belonging to the Mimosaceae or Rubiaceae family . Traditionally, catechu has been used in herbal preparations in Ayurveda, a traditional system of medicine in India . Some traditional medicinal uses include gastrointestinal disorders, wound healing, and as an antifertility agent.</data>
      <data key="d5">✅ SAFE: Likely Safe when used orally in amounts commonly found in foods. Catechu has Generally Recognized As Safe (GRAS) status for use in foods in the US . There is insufficient reliable information available about the safety of catechu when used orally in medicinal amounts or when used topically during pregnancy and lactation.</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Catnip">
      <data key="d0">supplement</data>
      <data key="d1">Nepeta cataria</data>
      <data key="d2">Cataire | Catmint | Catswort | Chataire | Field Balm | Herbe à Chat | Herbe aux Chats | Hierba Gatera | Menta de Gato | Menthe des Chats</data>
      <data key="d3">https://naturalmedicines.therapeuticresearch.com/Data/ProMonographs/Catnip</data>
      <data key="d4">Catnip is a perennial herb famous for the euphoric state it induces in cats. It is thought that the constituent cis-trans-nepetalcatone produces the characteristic stimulation observed when cats smell catnip . Although humans have used catnip to induce a euphoric high, whether or not this effect act</data>
      <data key="d5">⚠️ AVOID: Likely Unsafe when used orally. Catnip tea has been reported to have uterine stimulant properties ; avoid using. LACTATION : Insufficient reliable information available; avoid using.</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
