      <data key="d4">Celery is a biennial plant that grows to a height of 30-100 cm. It is found in Europe, western Asia, Africa, and the Americas . In foods, the stem can be consumed raw, as a juice, or as a cooked vegetable. The seed is sometimes used as a spice .</data>
      <data key="d5">⚠️ AVOID: Likely Unsafe when celery oil or seeds are used orally in larger amounts; celery might have uterine stimulant or abortifacient effects .</data>
