      <data key="d4">Chaga is a parasitic fungus that grows on the trunks of trees, especially birch, throughout Europe, Russia, Korea, northern China, parts of the United States, and Canada . Although often referred to as a mushroom, it is not a true mushroom. Chaga produces a woody growth, called a conk, to absorb nut</data>
