      <data key="d4">Chaparral is a shrub. It is native to South America, and also grows in the southwestern United States and northern Mexico . It is used by indigenous peoples for anti-inflammatory and anti-diabetic effects . Due to rare cases of kidney and liver toxicity, the U.S. Food and Drug Administration (FDA) a</data>
