    <node id="Chelation Therapy Products">
      <data key="d0">supplement</data>
      <data key="d1" />
      <data key="d2">2 | 3-Dimercaptopropane-1-Sulfonate | 2 | 3-Dimercaptosuccinic Acid | 3-Dimercaptosuccinate | Acide Éthylènediaminetétracétique | Ammonium Tetrathiomolybdate | BAL | BDET | BDETH2</data>
      <data key="d3">https://naturalmedicines.therapeuticresearch.com/Data/ProMonographs/Chelation-Therapy-Products</data>
      <data key="d4">Chelation therapy products are agents that bind metal ions, rendering the ions less toxic and easier to eliminate in the urine . Prescription chelation therapy products, either oral or parenteral, are used for the treatment of heavy metal toxicity, hypercalcemia, and other conditions following diagn</data>
      <data key="d5">⚠️ AVOID: Possibly Unsafe when unregulated chelation therapy products are used orally or parentally or when prescription chelation therapy products are used for unproven indications and/or in unapproved doses or routes of administration. The American College of Medical Toxicology and The American Academy of Clinical Toxicology recommend against the unapproved use of chelation therapy products . Chelation therapy products can have teratogenic effects and result in severe side effects including dehydration,</data>
      <data key="d6" />
