      <data key="d4">Chia is an annual herb which originated in Mexico and was cultivated by the Aztecs . Chia literally means "oily" . Chia is grown commercially in Central America and South America . It is primarily used for its seed, which is a rich source of omega-3 fatty acids .</data>
