    <node id="Chickweed">
      <data key="d0">supplement</data>
      <data key="d1">Stellaria media</data>
      <data key="d2">Capiqui | Fleur en Satin | Herbe de Langue | Hierba Gallinera | Morgeline | Mouron des Oiseaux | Mouron des oiseaux | Pamplina | Star Chickweed | Starweed</data>
      <data key="d3">https://naturalmedicines.therapeuticresearch.com/Data/ProMonographs/Chickweed</data>
      <data key="d4">Chickweed is a wild plant. While the plant is often used as a food, chickweed tea has also traditionally been used as a medicine . Traditional uses include scurvy, gastrointestinal disorders, musculoskeletal disorders, blood disorders, and wound healing.</data>
      <data key="d5">⚠️ AVOID: Likely Safe when used orally in the amounts commonly found in foods . There is insufficient reliable information available about the safety of chickweed when used orally in amounts greater than those found in food; avoid using.</data>
