      <data key="d4">Vitamin K refers to a group of chemically similar, fat-soluble compounds called naphthoquinones . The name vitamin K comes from the German word Koagulationsvitamin . Vitamin K1, also known as phytonadione or phylloquinone, is found in plants such as green leafy vegetables and vegetable oils . Vitami</data>
