      <data key="d4">Chondroitin sulfate is a glycosaminoglycan produced naturally in the body. It is formed by the 1-3 linkage of D-glucuronic acid to N-acetylgalactosamine. Chondroitin supplements are typically obtained from natural sources, such as shark and bovine cartilage, or produced synthetically .</data>
