      <data key="d3">https://naturalmedicines.therapeuticresearch.com/Data/ProMonographs/Cinchona</data>
      <data key="d4">Cinchona is an evergreen tree, growing up to 15 meters in height in its natural habitat on the eastern slopes of the Andes in Peru, Ecuador, and Colombia . It is cultivated in Africa, China, India, and Indonesia .</data>
      <data key="d5">⚠️ AVOID: Likely Unsafe when used orally. Cinchona is reported to have uterine stimulant and abortifacient activity, and to be fetotoxic and teratogenic, causing visual and auditory defects . Avoid using.</data>
