      <data key="d4">Citric acid is an alpha hydroxy acid. Alpha hydroxy acids are natural acids found in foods, including, but not limited to, citrus fruits, sugarcane, sour milk, apples, and grapes. Alpha hydroxy acids are commonly used in cosmetic products . Citric acid is sometimes found as an active ingredient, fla</data>
      <data key="d5">⚠️ AVOID: Likely Safe when citric acid is used orally in the amounts commonly found in foods. There is insufficient reliable information available about the safety of citric acid when used orally in larger amounts during pregnancy or lactation; avoid amounts greater than those found in foods.</data>
