      <data key="d3">https://naturalmedicines.therapeuticresearch.com/Data/ProMonographs/Clove</data>
      <data key="d4">Clove is a medium-sized tree that is native to the Maluku Islands in Indonesia . Due to the popular use of clove flower buds in tobacco products and as a culinary spice, clove is now grown in many other countries, including India, Malaysia, Sri Lanka, and Brazil . In Chinese and Ayurvedic medicine,</data>
      <data key="d5">⚠️ AVOID: Likely Safe when used orally in amounts found in foods . Clove, clove oil, and eugenol have Generally Recognized As Safe (GRAS) status for use in foods in the US . There is insufficient reliable information available about the safety of using clove in medicinal amounts during pregnancy and lactation; avoid using.</data>
