    <node id="Coca">
      <data key="d0">supplement</data>
      <data key="d1">Erythroxylum coca</data>
      <data key="d2">Bolivian Coca | Coca de Java | Coca Péruvienne | Cocaïer | Cocaine Plant | Gu Ko Yi | Health Inca Tea | Huanuco Coca | Inca Health Tea | Inca Tea</data>
      <data key="d3">https://naturalmedicines.therapeuticresearch.com/Data/ProMonographs/Coca</data>
      <data key="d4">Coca is a plant that is native to western South America, specifically the Andean region. The leaves have been used widely by South American indigenous tribes . The drug cocaine was originally isolated from the coca leaf . Decocainized coca extract is sometimes used as a flavoring in foods and drinks</data>
      <data key="d5">⚠️ AVOID: Unsafe when inhaled or used orally. Coca, and the constituent cocaine, are contraindicated due to abortifacient and teratogenic effects . Coca use is also associated with a high incidence of sudden infant death syndrome (SIDS) .</data>
      <data key="d6" />
