      <data key="d2">Aceite de Higado de Bacalao | Aceite de hígado de bacalao | Acides Gras N-3 | Acides Gras Oméga 3 | Acides Gras Polyinsaturés | Cod Oil | Fish Liver Oil | Halibut Liver Oil | Huile de Foie | Huile de Foie de Flétan</data>
      <data key="d3">https://naturalmedicines.therapeuticresearch.com/Data/ProMonographs/Cod-Liver-Oil</data>
      <data key="d4">Cod liver oil is obtained from fresh livers of Atlantic cod and other species of the family Gadidae. It is a rich source of omega-3 polyunsaturated fatty acids and contains significant amounts of vitamins A and D . Cod liver oil products sold as dietary supplements in the US are not standardized and</data>
      <data key="d5">✅ SAFE: Possibly Safe when used orally and appropriately in doses providing no more than the recommended dietary allowances (RDAs) of vitamins A and D. For vitamin A, the RDAs are 770 mcg (2567 units of retinol) daily for pregnant women over 18 years of age, and 750 mcg (2500 units of retinol) daily for pregnant teenagers 14 years to 18 years of age . For vitamin D, the RDA is 15 mcg (600 units) daily for pregnant women of all ages . In clinical research, cod liver oil (Peter Möller, Oslo, Norway) 10 mL</data>
