    <node id="Coleus">
      <data key="d0">supplement</data>
      <data key="d1">Plectranthus barbatus</data>
      <data key="d2">13-epoxy-1alpha | 17beta-acetoxy-8 | 6beta | 9alpha-trihydroxylabd-14-en-11-one | Borforsin | Cóleo | Colforsin | Colforsine | Forskohlii | Forskolin</data>
      <data key="d3">https://naturalmedicines.therapeuticresearch.com/Data/ProMonographs/Coleus</data>
      <data key="d4">Coleus (Plectranthus barbatus) is a member of the mint family and is native plant of Nepal, India, and Thailand . The root of coleus is commonly used in Ayurvedic medicine and in Indian foods. Traditionally it is used as a diuretic, a blood purifier, and to decrease blood pressure .</data>
      <data key="d5">⚠️ AVOID: Possibly Unsafe when used orally. Evidence from animal research suggests that high doses of coleus can inhibit embryo implantation and/or delay fetal development ; avoid using.</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
