    <node id="Collagen Peptides">
      <data key="d0">supplement</data>
      <data key="d1">Collagen peptides</data>
      <data key="d2">Collagen Hydrolysate | Collagen Peptidesi | Collagène Dénaturé | Collagène Hydrolysé | Collagène Marin Hydrolysé | Denatured Collagen | Hydrolised Collagen | Hydrolysed Collagen | Hydrolyzed Collagen | Hydrolyzed Collagen Protein</data>
      <data key="d3">https://naturalmedicines.therapeuticresearch.com/Data/ProMonographs/Collagen-Peptides</data>
      <data key="d4">Collagen peptides, which are also commonly referred to as hydrolyzed collagen and collagen hydrolysate, are small peptides (average molecular weight 3.3 kDa) derived from collagen, the primary structural protein in ligaments, tendons, skin, and bones. The most common method used to produce collagen</data>
      <data key="d5">⚠️ AVOID: &amp; LACTATION: Insufficient reliable information available; avoid using.</data>
