    <node id="Collagen Type I (Native)">
      <data key="d0">supplement</data>
      <data key="d1" />
      <data key="d2">Atelocollagen type I | Colágeno tipo I (nativo) | Collagen Type I | Collagène de Type I (Natif) | Native Collagen Type I | Native Type I Collagen | Type I Collagen | Undenatured Collagen Type I | Undenatured Type I Collagen</data>
      <data key="d3">https://naturalmedicines.therapeuticresearch.com/Data/ProMonographs/Collagen-Type-I-native</data>
      <data key="d4">Collagen type I (native) is the main collagen in skin, tendon, ligaments, and bone. It plays a major role as a scaffold in normal wound healing. It is composed of three polypeptide chains in a triple helix structure . Collagen type I (native) is commonly used to support healthy skin, hair, and nails</data>
      <data key="d5">⚠️ AVOID: Insufficient reliable information is available; avoid using.</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Collagen Type Ii (Native)">
      <data key="d0">supplement</data>
      <data key="d1">Collagen type</data>
      <data key="d2">Chicken Collagen Type II | Chicken Type II Collagen | Colágeno de Pollo | Colágeno Tipo II (nativo) | Collagen II | Collagen Type II | Collagène de Poulet | Collagène de Type II | Collagène de type II (natif) | Collagène de Type II de Cartilage de Poulet</data>
      <data key="d3">https://naturalmedicines.therapeuticresearch.com/Data/ProMonographs/Collagen-Type-II-native</data>
      <data key="d4">Collagen type II (native) is the main structural protein in cartilage. It is also found in other types of connective tissue. Most supplemental collagen type II comes from chicken sources, although some comes from bovine sources . This monograph discusses only native (undenatured) collagen type II.</data>
      <data key="d5">⚠️ AVOID: Insufficient reliable information available; avoid using.</data>
      <data key="d6" />
