      <data key="d4">Colocynth is a plant that commonly grows in East Asia, as well as North Africa and the Middle East. The fruit of colocynth, which looks like a small watermelon, has been used medicinally . Due to reports of toxicity, colocynth was banned by the US Food and Drug Administration (FDA) in 1991 . Unsafe</data>
      <data key="d5">⚠️ AVOID: Unsafe when used orally due to severe gastrointestinal toxicity ; avoid using.</data>
      <data key="d6" />
