      <data key="d3">https://naturalmedicines.therapeuticresearch.com/Data/ProMonographs/Comfrey</data>
      <data key="d4">Comfrey is a perennial herb found in Europe, Asia, and North America . The plant has pale yellow or purple flowers and long rough leaves. Comfrey leaf, rhizome, and root are used medicinally . It has traditionally been used topically as an analgesic, astringent, and for wound healing. The FDA has re</data>
      <data key="d5">⚠️ AVOID: Likely Unsafe when used orally or topically. In addition to hepatotoxicity and possible carcinogenicity, the pyrrolizidine alkaloids (PAs) in comfrey might be teratogenic. PAs are absorbed through the skin .</data>
      <data key="d6" />
