      <data key="d2">Acide Linoléique Conjugué | Acide Linoléique Conjugué (ALC) | Acide Linoléique Conjugué Cis-9 | trans-11 | Acide Linoléique Conjugué trans-10 | cis-12 | Acido Linoleico Conjugado | Ácido linoleico conjugado (CLA) | ALC | CLA</data>
      <data key="d3">https://naturalmedicines.therapeuticresearch.com/Data/ProMonographs/Conjugated-Linoleic-Acid-CLA</data>
      <data key="d4">Conjugated linoleic acid (CLA) refers to a group of conjugated dienoic isomers of linoleic acid . An average diet supplies 15-174 mg of CLA daily, primarily from milk, milk products, and meat from cows, goats, and other ruminants . Most dietary supplements containing CLA are made from safflower oil.</data>
      <data key="d5">⚠️ AVOID: Likely Safe when used orally in amounts found in foods . There is insufficient reliable information available about the safety of CLA when used in medicinal amounts during pregnancy or lactation; avoid using.</data>
      <data key="d6" />
