      <data key="d4">Coral is a type of marine invertebrate. Like sea anemone, coral has a simple polyp structure. Coral polyps can exist as individual entities or in colonies, which may grow large enough to form reefs. Coral polyps secrete calcium carbonate, which forms a hard exoskeleton .</data>
