      <data key="d3">https://naturalmedicines.therapeuticresearch.com/Data/ProMonographs/Vitamin-B6</data>
      <data key="d4">Vitamin B6 is a member of the vitamin B family. It is present in many foods including cereal grains, legumes, vegetables, liver, meat, and eggs . Pyridoxine, pyridoxal, and pyridoxamine are all forms of vitamin B6 and are considered to be equivalent in the human body . Dietary supplements containing</data>
      <data key="d5">✅ SAFE: Likely Safe when used orally and appropriately. A special sustained-release product providing vitamin B6 (pyridoxine) 75 mg daily is FDA-approved for use in pregnancy. Vitamin B6 (pyridoxine) is also considered a first-line treatment for nausea and vomiting in pregnancy by the American College of Obstetrics and Gynecology . However, it should not be used long-term or without medical supervision and close monitoring. The tolerable upper intake level (UL) refers to vitamin B6 in the form of pyrido</data>
