      <data key="d4">Creatine is an amine that plays a role in skeletal muscle energy metabolism. It is naturally produced in the body from amino acids in the kidney and liver. It is also found in the diet, most often in red meat and seafood. Ninety-five percent of creatine is stored in skeletal muscle, with the remaind</data>
