      <data key="d3">https://naturalmedicines.therapeuticresearch.com/Data/ProMonographs/Dusty-Miller</data>
      <data key="d4">Dusty miller is a plant that is sometimes used as medicine. Traditional uses include respiratory illness, cataracts, and other eye problems. Dusty miller contains hepatotoxic pyrrolizidine alkaloid (PA) constituents, which are likely unsafe when used orally or topically on broken skin .</data>
      <data key="d5">⚠️ AVOID: Likely Unsafe when used orally. Dusty miller preparations containing hepatotoxic pyrrolizidine alkaloid (PA) constituents might be teratogenic and hepatotoxic . There is insufficient reliable information available about the safety of dusty miller products that do not contain hepatotoxic PAs when used during pregnancy.</data>
