      <data key="d4">English ivy is a woody, evergreen climber that is native to many parts of Europe and southwest Asia. In the United States, English ivy is often used as a landscaping groundcover despite the fact that it is an invasive species considered to be a noxious weed. As a medicine, English ivy is most often</data>
      <data key="d5">⚠️ AVOID: Insufficient reliable information available; avoid using. A small retrospective study suggests that taking English ivy leaf extract at an unknown dose or duration during pregnancy is not associated with changes in pregnancy duration, the rate of preterm birth, infant health complications, or infant deaths . However, due to its small size, retrospective design, and insufficient information regarding dose and duration, further research is needed to determine the safety of English ivy during pregna</data>
