      <data key="d4">Eurycoma longifolia is a tall, slender, shrubby tree which grows in sandy soil, usually on jungle slopes in Southeast Asian countries . Eurycoma longifolia is a protected species in Malaysia where it has a long history of use for malaria, as an aphrodisiac, and for male virility. .</data>
      <data key="d5">⚠️ AVOID: Insufficient reliable information available; avoid using. Animal research suggests that there are no negative effects of Eurycoma longifolia on the offspring . However, research in humans is lacking.</data>
