      <data key="d3">https://naturalmedicines.therapeuticresearch.com/Data/ProMonographs/Evening-Primrose</data>
      <data key="d4">Evening primrose is a biennial plant native to North and South America and widespread throughout Europe and parts of Asia . In North America, the plant blooms from June to September and has yellow flowers that open at sunset and close during the day . The leaves can be cooked and eaten as greens; th</data>
      <data key="d5">✅ SAFE: Possibly Safe when evening primrose oil is used orally and appropriately. In small studies of evening primrose oil for pre-eclampsia, 4 grams has been used orally daily for up to 10 weeks during pregnancy with apparent safety . ...when evening primrose oil is used orally or intravaginally to improve cervical ripening. Evening primrose oil has been used safely during the last 1-3 weeks of pregnancy to improve cervical ripening . Intravaginally, evening primrose oil 500-1000 mg as either a single</data>
      <data key="d6" />
