      <data key="d4">During fish therapy, or ichthyotherapy, a specific species of fish (Garra rufa) feeds on dead skin cells . Garra rufa, commonly called doctor fish, are toothless bottom dwellers. In their natural habitat, they feed on small organisms that live on rocks. Garra rufa is typically placed in pools or con</data>
