      <data key="d3">https://naturalmedicines.therapeuticresearch.com/Data/ProMonographs/Flaxseed</data>
      <data key="d4">Flax is a food and fiber crop . Flaxseeds contain phytoestrogens, as well as soluble fiber and oil. The fiber is found in the seed coat gum . Flaxseed oil is approximately 55% alpha-linolenic acid (ALA), an essential omega-3 fatty acid. This makes flaxseed oil one of the richest food sources of ALA</data>
      <data key="d5">⚠️ AVOID: Possibly Unsafe when used orally. Flaxseed can have mild estrogenic effects. Theoretically, this might adversely affect pregnancy ; however, there is no reliable clinical evidence about the effects of flaxseed on pregnancy outcomes.</data>
