      <data key="d3">https://naturalmedicines.therapeuticresearch.com/Data/ProMonographs/Flaxseed-Oil</data>
      <data key="d4">Flaxseed oil is derived from the flaxseed. Flaxseed oil contains fatty acids, of which approximately 55% is alpha-linolenic acid (ALA), an essential omega-3 fatty acid . CHILDREN: Possibly Safe when used orally and appropriately, short-term. Some evidence suggests that flaxseed oil, providing 200 mg</data>
      <data key="d5">✅ SAFE: Possibly Safe when used orally and appropriately for medicinal purposes, short-term. Although flaxseed oil has been used with apparent safety in clinical research in doses of 1-2 grams daily for up to 6 weeks , some population research has found that consuming flaxseed oil during the second and third trimesters of pregnancy is associated with a four-fold increased risk of premature birth .</data>
