      <data key="d4">Fo-ti is a root of a climbing plant native to east Asia and some parts of North America . It is one of the most popular herbs used in traditional Chinese medicine and is officially listed in the Chinese Pharmacopoeia . CHILDREN: Possibly Unsafe when used orally. Fo-ti has been linked to several case</data>
      <data key="d5">⚠️ AVOID: Possibly Unsafe when used orally. Fo-ti contains anthraquinone constituents, which can exert a stimulant laxative effect. Bulk-forming or emollient laxatives are preferred in pregnancy . Fo-ti has also been linked to several cases of liver damage . There is insufficient reliable information available about the safety of fo-ti when used topically during pregnancy.</data>
