      <data key="d4">Gamma-aminobutyric acid (GABA) is a natural non-protein amino acid. It is produced in the brain by the decarboxylation of glutamate . In the central nervous system, endogenous GABA is the main inhibitory neurotransmitter . There is interest in using exogenous GABA as a dietary supplement and in food</data>
