      <data key="d3">https://naturalmedicines.therapeuticresearch.com/Data/ProMonographs/Glycerol</data>
      <data key="d4">Glycerol is a trivalent alcohol that occurs naturally in the body. It is used as a solvent, emollient, pharmaceutical agent, and sweetening agent . The World Anti-Doping Agency (WADA) prohibits the use of glycerol due to its potential to increase blood volume and therefore mask blood doping . CHILDR</data>
