      <data key="d4">Glyconutrients is a term that is used to describe dietary supplements composed of gums and polysaccharides. It is suggested that these carbohydrates supply the body with simple sugars (monosaccharides) claimed to be essential: glucose, galactose, mannose, fucose, xylose, N-acetyl glucosamine, N-acet</data>
