      <data key="d4">Vitis vinifera is a grapevine species indigenous to parts of Europe and Asia . Thousands of cultivars of this grape species exist and are commonly used in wine production, as well as for table grapes and raisins . Vitis labrusca, commonly referred to as the Concord grape, is believed to have been do</data>
