      <data key="d3">https://naturalmedicines.therapeuticresearch.com/Data/ProMonographs/Guar-Gum</data>
      <data key="d4">Guar gum is a water soluble, gel-forming fiber extracted from seeds of the guar plant (Cyamopsis tetragonoloba) . The plant is primarily grown in Pakistan and parts of India. Guar gum is widely used as a food-thickening agent. It is also found in dietary supplements . CHILDREN: Possibly Safe when us</data>
      <data key="d5">✅ SAFE: Possibly Safe when used orally and appropriately in medicinal amounts. Guar gum has been safely used at doses of 5-15 grams daily for up to 4 weeks during pregnancy .</data>
