      <data key="d4">Guava is a tropical plant native to Central and South America. The fruit, sometimes called the "poor man's apple", is commonly consumed fresh or processed into beverages, jams, and other foods . All parts of the plant are used in medicine, although the leaf is the most commonly used . KEY HIGHLIGHTS</data>
