      <data key="d2">18:1 n-9 (synonyms: (9Z)-Octadec-9-Enoic Acid | 9-Octadecenoic Acid | Cis-9-Octadecenoic Acid | Octadec-9-Enoic Acid | Octadecenoic Acid) | Acide oléique | Ácido oleico</data>
      <data key="d3">https://naturalmedicines.therapeuticresearch.com/Data/ProMonographs/Oleic-Acid</data>
      <data key="d4">Oleic acid is a monounsaturated omega-9 fatty acid that is a non-essential fatty acid. It is found in the highest amounts in olive oil, canola oil, high-oleic acid canola oil, or high-oleic acid sunflower oil, as well as diets rich in these oils, such as the Mediterranean diet . The US Food and Drug</data>
