      <data key="d4">Hemp is a plant native to western and central Asia that has been used for food, fiber, and medicine for at least 3,000 years in China and the Middle East. It is the same species (Cannabis sativa) as the cannabis plant, but the two plants are differentiated by their delta-9-tetrahydrocannabinol (THC)</data>
