      <data key="d3">https://naturalmedicines.therapeuticresearch.com/Data/ProMonographs/Homeopathy</data>
      <data key="d4">Homeopathy is an alternative medicine practice that is based on the theory that symptoms can be treated by using highly diluted substances that cause the same symptoms when used in larger doses . However, most homeopathic preparations are so dilute that they contain little or no active ingredient. T</data>
      <data key="d5">⚠️ AVOID: Insufficient reliable information available; avoid using. Since most homeopathic preparations contain little or no active ingredient, it is unlikely that most homeopathic preparations would have an adverse effect during pregnancy or breast-feeding. However, it is important to recognize the possibility of homeopathic products being mislabeled and containing active and potentially dangerous substances that are not homeopathic dilutions . Also, the inactive ingredients in some homeopathic preparati</data>
