      <data key="d4">Homotaurine is an amino acid that is not involved in protein synthesis, but is an analog of the inhibitory neurotransmitter gamma-aminobutyric acid (GABA). It is found naturally in some types of algae . Although homotaurine was under development as a prescription drug for Alzheimer disease, the FDA</data>
