      <data key="d3">https://naturalmedicines.therapeuticresearch.com/Data/ProMonographs/Hypnotherapy</data>
      <data key="d4">Hypnotherapy is the use of hypnosis for therapeutic purposes . Hypnosis is a state of consciousness with a reduced peripheral awareness and an increased capacity for response to suggestion or instruction . Hypnotherapy may involve self-hypnosis using an audio-recording and/or sessions with a hypnoth</data>
      <data key="d5">✅ SAFE: Possibly Safe when hypnotherapy is used appropriately. Use of self-hypnosis during labor following teaching sessions during pregnancy has not been shown to affect birthweight, well-being of the newborn, admission or re-admission for neonatal care, maternal stay in the hospital, readmission to hospital, lactation establishment, or ability to care for the infant . However, the use of hypnotherapy should not delay the time to diagnosis or treatment with more proven therapies.</data>
