      <data key="d3">https://naturalmedicines.therapeuticresearch.com/Data/ProMonographs/Jewelweed</data>
      <data key="d4">Jewelweed is a plant native to parts of the United States and Canada. It is often found in wet woodland areas and riverbanks. The native species is Impatiens capensis. It produces orange or yellow flowers. The species Impatiens balsamina is native to China and produces pink or purple flowers .</data>
