      <data key="d4">Jojoba ( Simmondsia chinensis ) is a shrub native to deserts in Arizona, California and Mexico and is also found in some arid African countries . The oil (or liquid wax) in jojoba seeds contains extremely long (C36-C46) straight chain fatty acids in the form of wax esters, as opposed to triglyceride</data>
