      <data key="d2">Boerenkool | Borecole | Chou Fourrager | Chou frisé | Chou Kale | Col rizada | Col Rizada | Kale Frisé | Kale Frisé Sibérien | Kale Leaf</data>
      <data key="d3">https://naturalmedicines.therapeuticresearch.com/Data/ProMonographs/Kale</data>
      <data key="d4">Kale is a dark, leafy vegetable that has green or purple leaves . It is similar to cruciferous vegetables such as broccoli, cauliflower, and collard . It is believed to have originated in the eastern Mediterranean and to have been used as a food crop since 2000 BC . There is interest in its use as a</data>
      <data key="d5">⚠️ AVOID: Likely Safe when used orally in amounts commonly found in foods. There is insufficient reliable information available about the safety of kale when used orally in medicinal amounts; avoid use.</data>
