      <data key="d3">https://naturalmedicines.therapeuticresearch.com/Data/ProMonographs/Kaolin</data>
      <data key="d4">Kaolin is a type of clay. The main component of kaolin is aluminum silicate. Historically, kaolin was used in combination with pectin (Kaopectate) for diarrhea. However, this product has been reformulated without kaolin in the US . In parts of Africa, kaolin is consumed, particularly by pregnant pat</data>
      <data key="d5">⚕️ CONSULT PHYSICIAN: In parts of Africa, kaolin is consumed, particularly by pregnant patients, to treat nausea, abdominal pain, diarrhea, and excessive salivation, and also in the belief that it will cause the baby to have softer, lighter skin .</data>
