      <data key="d4">In 1919, William F. Koch MD, PhD, developed a substance he named "synthetic anti-toxin," which later became known as "glyoxylide." The treatment was marketed under the label of the "Christian Medical Research League." Koch proposed that a single toxin caused cancer, and that cancer could be prevente</data>
