    <node id="Krill Oil">
      <data key="d0">supplement</data>
      <data key="d1" />
      <data key="d2">Aceite de Krill | Aceite de krill | Acide Docosahexaénoïque | Acides Gras N-3 | Acides Gras Oméga 3 | Acides Gras Polyinsaturés | Acides Gras W3 | Antarctic Krill Oil | Concentré de Protéines Marines | DHA</data>
      <data key="d3">https://naturalmedicines.therapeuticresearch.com/Data/ProMonographs/Krill-Oil</data>
      <data key="d4">Krill are small, shrimp-like crustaceans which serve as a primary food source for some types of marine life . Krill ingest algae, which provide omega-3 fatty acids. Thus, krill oil contains significant amounts of the omega-3 fatty acids eicosapentaenoic acid (EPA) and docosahexaenoic acid (DHA) . CH</data>
      <data key="d5">⚠️ AVOID: Insufficient reliable information available; avoid using.</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
