      <data key="d3">https://naturalmedicines.therapeuticresearch.com/Data/ProMonographs/Kudzu</data>
      <data key="d4">Kudzu is a climbing, perennial vine with hairy, rusty-brown stems, a large tuberous root, and a sweet scent . Kudzu is native to Asia, including Thailand, China, and India . It is now invasive in the United States . Kudzu is traditionally used for various conditions including tinnitus, gastrointesti</data>
      <data key="d5">⚠️ AVOID: Insufficient reliable information available; avoid using.</data>
