      <data key="d4">Lactobacillus acidophilus is a species of lactic acid-producing, gram-positive, rod-shaped, homofermentive, anaerobic bacteria. L. acidophilus is indigenous to the human and animal intestinal tract, as well as the mouth and vagina, and is found in foods such as sourdough and wine. Specific strains o</data>
      <data key="d5">✅ SAFE: Possibly Safe when used orally and appropriately. A combination of Lactobacillus acidophilus, Lacticaseibacillus casei, and Bifidobacterium bifidum has been used with apparent safety for 6 weeks, starting at 24-28 weeks' gestation .</data>
