      <data key="d4">Lactoferrin is a type of glycoprotein that binds to iron. It is found in human and animal colostrum, nasal, intestinal, and genital secretions, and milk, tears, saliva, and seminal fluid. It is also secreted from neutrophils . Lactoferrin can be extracted from human or bovine milk. The recombinant h</data>
