      <data key="d3">https://naturalmedicines.therapeuticresearch.com/Data/ProMonographs/L-Arginine</data>
      <data key="d4">L-arginine is an amino acid necessary for protein synthesis. It is found naturally in foods such as red meat, poultry, fish, and dairy products . L-arginine was first isolated in 1886 by the Swiss chemist Ernst Schultz from the extract of a lupin seedling . Coronavirus disease 2019 (COVID-19) : Desp</data>
      <data key="d5">✅ SAFE: Possibly Safe when used orally and appropriately, short-term. L-arginine 12 grams daily for 2 days has been used with apparent safety in pregnancy during the third trimester . L-arginine 3 grams daily has been taken safely during the second and/or third trimesters . ...when used intravenously and appropriately, short-term. Intravenous L-arginine 20-30 grams daily has been used safely in pregnancy for up to 5 days .</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
