      <data key="d4">L-carnitine is an amino acid derivative. It is naturally found in the body . L-carnitine is made in the human brain, liver, and kidneys from the amino acids lysine and methionine . Most of the daily L-carnitine requirement is provided by the diet, especially from dairy products and red meat, as well</data>
