      <data key="d4">L-citrulline is a non-essential alpha-amino acid. It is produced naturally in the body and is metabolized to the amino acid L-arginine . The name citrulline is derived from watermelon, Citrullus vulgaris, from which it was first isolated . CHILDREN: Possibly Safe when used orally and appropriately.</data>
