      <data key="d4">Lily-of-the-valley is a fragrant and poisonous plant that is native to Europe. It also grows in the U.S. and northern Asia . Lily-of-the-valley contains many cardiac glycosides and is most commonly used for cardiovascular conditions. Note that digoxin is a safer alternative than non-standardized lil</data>
