      <data key="d4">Nutmeg and mace are two commonly used spices originating from the same tree, Myristica fragrans. The tree is indigenous to the Banda Islands of Indonesia, and is now cultivated in other tropical regions, such as Malaysia and the Caribbean . Mace is derived from the aril (seed covering) of Myristica</data>
