      <data key="d4">Maggots are living fly larvae that consume decaying or necrotic tissue. Typically, larvae of the green bottle fly (Lucilia sericata) are used for therapeutic purposes, but related species such as Lucilia cuprina have also been used . Maggot therapy is a type of biosurgery or biotherapy that uses liv</data>
