      <data key="d4">Radish is a perennial plant native to Japan and China. The root and leaves are commonly eaten as a food. The leaf, root, and seed are used as medicine . Traditionally radish has been used for biliary disorders, constipation, cough, diarrhea, dyspepsia, jaundice, and liver disease .</data>
