      <data key="d4">Magnet therapy refers to the placement of static or pulsating magnets on or near the body at the site of a problematic area, often related to pain. Worldwide sales of therapeutic magnets is estimated at over $5 billion annually . In the United States, the market is about $500 million.</data>
