      <data key="d4">Mallow is an annual plant native to Europe, North Africa, and Asia. It grows wild in fields and hedgerows. The ancient Greeks and Romans used mallow for its emollient and laxative properties, and it is used for cooking in Turkey in the Central Anatolia region . It has traditionally been used for its</data>
