      <data key="d3">https://naturalmedicines.therapeuticresearch.com/Data/ProMonographs/Manganese</data>
      <data key="d4">Manganese is the twelfth most abundant element in the earth's crust. It is also an essential nutrient involved in normal cell growth, generation of the immune response, glucose regulation, and metabolism of carbohydrates, lipids, and proteins . Manganese acts as a cofactor in several metabolic and e</data>
      <data key="d5">✅ SAFE: Likely Safe when used orally and appropriately. Manganese is safe when used in doses below the tolerable upper intake level (UL) of 11 mg daily during pregnancy or lactation in those aged 19 or older. However, those under 19 years of age should limit doses to less than 9 mg daily .</data>
