      <data key="d1">Rhododendron tomentosum</data>
      <data key="d2">James' Tea | Lède des Marais | Ledi Palustris Herba | Lédon des Marais | Ledum Silvestre | Marsh Cistus | Moth Herb | Northern Labrador Tea | Petit Thé du Labrador | Romarin Sauvage</data>
      <data key="d3">https://naturalmedicines.therapeuticresearch.com/Data/ProMonographs/Marsh-Labrador-Tea</data>
      <data key="d4">Marsh Labrador tea is prepared from the leaves of a small, evergreen shrub, Rhododendron tomentosum, that grows in nutrient-poor, acidic soils of humid areas in North America, Europe, and Asia. Traditionally, it has been used by the indigenous peoples of North America as an abortifacient, diaphoreti</data>
      <data key="d5">⚠️ AVOID: Likely Unsafe when used orally; avoid using . Marsh Labrador tea is considered to be a potential uterine stimulant and abortifacient .</data>
      <data key="d6" />
