      <data key="d4">The term "melanotan" describes two synthetic products known as melanotan-I and melanotan-II. These products were originally developed as analogues to alpha-melanocyte-stimulating hormone (alpha-MSH), an endogenous peptide hormone responsible for pigmentation of the skin. Melanotan-I, also known as a</data>
