      <data key="d2">Crystalline DMSO | Dimethyl Sulfone MSM | Diméthylsulfone | DMSO2 | Methyl Sulfone | Methyl Sulfonyl Methane | Methyl Sulphonyl Methane | Méthyle Sulfonyle Méthane | Méthyle Sulphonyle Méthane | Méthylsufonlylméthane (MSM)</data>
      <data key="d3">https://naturalmedicines.therapeuticresearch.com/Data/ProMonographs/Methylsulfonylmethane-MSM</data>
      <data key="d4">Methylsulfonylmethane (MSM) is a naturally occurring compound found in some green plants, algae, fruits, vegetables, grains, and milk, as well as the urine of humans and animals . It is a metabolite of dimethylsulfoxide (DMSO), produced by oxidation . In the body, about 15% of ingested DMSO is conve</data>
