      <data key="d3">https://naturalmedicines.therapeuticresearch.com/Data/ProMonographs/Monolaurin</data>
      <data key="d4">Monolaurin, a fatty acid ester, is the monoglyceride derivative of lauric acid. It occurs naturally in the blood as a product of lipid metabolism, and is also found in coconut oil and in human milk . It is used commercially as a surfactant .</data>
      <data key="d5">ℹ️ No pregnancy data available. Consult your physician.</data>
