      <data key="d3">https://naturalmedicines.therapeuticresearch.com/Data/ProMonographs/Mormon-Tea</data>
      <data key="d4">Mormon tea is an evergreen shrub that contains large amounts of tannins. Despite being in the Ephedra genus, Mormon tea contains no ephedrine or other alkaloids . Traditional uses of Mormon tea include asthma, sexually transmitted infections, and as a diuretic.</data>
      <data key="d5">⚠️ AVOID: Insufficient reliable information available; avoid using in amounts greater than those commonly found in foods.</data>
