      <data key="d2">Aconite Cake-Separated Moxibustion | Acu-Moxi | Acu-Moxibustion | Angelica-Cake Moxibustion | Bird-Pecking Moxibustion | Cake-Separated Mild-Warm Moxibustion | Cake-Separated Moxibustion | Chinetsukyu (Japanese) | Circling Moxibustion | Cone Moxibustion</data>
      <data key="d3">https://naturalmedicines.therapeuticresearch.com/Data/ProMonographs/Moxibustion</data>
      <data key="d4">Moxibustion is a therapeutic method in traditional Chinese medicine (TCM). The method involves burning an herb, usually mugwort (Artemisia vulgaris), above the skin or on the acupuncture points to introduce heat into an acupuncture point for therapeutic effects. It may be performed by burning a cone</data>
      <data key="d5">⚠️ AVOID: Possibly Unsafe when used during pregnancy. While moxibustion has been used with apparent safety during pregnancy in most clinical studies , some clinical evidence suggests that moxibustion may be associated with premature birth, premature membrane rupture, increased rate of contractions, abdominal pain due to contractions, placental bleeding, reduced or increased fetal movement, and reduced fetal heart rate .</data>
