      <data key="d3">https://naturalmedicines.therapeuticresearch.com/Data/ProMonographs/Myrrh</data>
      <data key="d4">Myrrh is the yellow, aromatic, oleo-gum resin exuded from fissures or cuts in the bark of certain Commiphora trees . The species used medicinally is Commiphora myrrham, which is native to Ethiopia, Somalia, Northern Kenya, and some Asian countries . While myrrh is used worldwide, it is particularly</data>
      <data key="d5">⚠️ AVOID: Likely Unsafe when used orally. Myrrh stimulates uterine tone and blood flow and may have an abortifacient effect . There is insufficient reliable information available about the safety of the topical use of myrrh during pregnancy.</data>
