      <data key="d4">Northern prickly ash is a woody shrub native to eastern parts of North America. It is most often found in rocky woods and along streams. Native American healers used its bark, berries, and roots as medicine. Traditionally, northern prickly ash was used to treat infections, rheumatic conditions, sore</data>
