      <data key="d3">https://naturalmedicines.therapeuticresearch.com/Data/ProMonographs/Oleander</data>
      <data key="d4">Oleander is a flowering shrub found mainly in temperate and sub-tropical climates . It contains toxic cardiac glycosides. Accidental and intentional deaths have occurred after oleander ingestion . Coronavirus disease 2019 (COVID-19) : Oleander extract has been promoted for use in the treatment of CO</data>
      <data key="d5">⚠️ AVOID: Likely Unsafe when used orally. Oleander has been reported to have abortifacient properties . Also, maternal ingestion of oleander seeds during pregnancy has led to fetal toxicity . There is insufficient reliable information available about the safety of topical use of oleander during pregnancy and lactation; avoid using.</data>
