    <node id="Oolong Tea">
      <data key="d0">supplement</data>
      <data key="d1">Camellia sinensis</data>
      <data key="d2">Brown Tea | Camélia Chinois | Dragon Noir | EGCG | Epigallo Catechin Gallate | Epigallocatechin Gallate | Épigallocatéchine Gallate | Té Oolong | Tea | Tea Oolong</data>
      <data key="d3">https://naturalmedicines.therapeuticresearch.com/Data/ProMonographs/Oolong-Tea</data>
      <data key="d4">Oolong tea is made from Camellia sinensis, a woody plant from which a variety of teas, including green tea and black tea, are produced . Oolong tea is fermented for longer than green tea but for less time than black tea . It is largely produced and consumed in China . CHILDREN: Possibly Safe when us</data>
      <data key="d5">✅ SAFE: Possibly Safe when used orally in moderate amounts. Due to the caffeine content of oolong tea, mothers should closely monitor their intake to ensure moderate consumption. Fetal blood concentrations of caffeine approximate maternal concentrations . Use of caffeine in pregnancy is controversial; however, moderate consumption has not been associated with clinically important adverse fetal effects .</data>
      <data key="d6" />
