      <data key="d3">https://naturalmedicines.therapeuticresearch.com/Data/ProMonographs/Oregano</data>
      <data key="d4">Oregano is a perennial herb which grows to between 1-3 feet tall and has olive-green leaves and purple flowers. As a member of the Lamiaceae family, it is closely related to mint, thyme, marjoram, basil, sage, and lavender. Oregano is native to warm-temperate western and southwestern Europe and the</data>
