      <data key="d4">Oregon grape is a perennial plant native to the western coast of North America. It grows wild in Europe, as well as in North and South America . Oregon grape has a history of use in American folk medicine for inflammatory skin conditions, including psoriasis and syphilis . CHILDREN: Likely Unsafe wh</data>
      <data key="d5">⚠️ AVOID: Likely Unsafe when used orally. Berberine, a constituent of Oregon grape, is thought to cross the placenta and may cause harm to the fetus. Kernicterus has developed in newborn infants exposed to berberine .</data>
