      <data key="d4">Ornithine is a nonessential amino acid that is not used in protein synthesis. In the body, it is produced in the urea cycle as part of the disposal of excess nitrogen during the breakdown of L-arginine by the enzyme arginase. In this cycle, ornithine is recycled to citrulline and eventually arginine</data>
