      <data key="d4">Palm oil is an edible vegetable oil derived from the fleshy fruit of oil palm trees native to West Africa (E. guineensis) or South America (E. oleifera) . Crude or virgin palm oil, obtained by direct compression of the fruit, is called "red palm oil" due to its high beta-carotene content. Refined pa</data>
