      <data key="d4">Panax is a genus of slow-growing, deciduous plants that includes 13 different species . While many of these species may be referred to as "ginseng," typically the term "ginseng" is associated with the species Panax ginseng . Panax ginseng grows in Korea, northeastern China, and far-eastern Siberia .</data>
