      <data key="d2">Bis-pantothenamidoethyl Disulfide | D-Pantethine | D-Pantéthine | Pantesin | Panteteina | Pantetheine | Pantéthine | Pantethine Octahydrate | Pantetina | Pantomin</data>
      <data key="d3">https://naturalmedicines.therapeuticresearch.com/Data/ProMonographs/Pantethine</data>
      <data key="d4">Pantethine is a chemical that occurs naturally in the body; it is derived from pantothenic acid (vitamin B5) . It is a key constituent of coenzyme A (CoA) and acyl carrier protein . It is marketed in Japan and China as a prescription drug for hyperlipidemia.</data>
      <data key="d5">⚠️ AVOID: Insufficient reliable information available; avoid using.</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
