      <data key="d3">https://naturalmedicines.therapeuticresearch.com/Data/ProMonographs/Pau-DArco</data>
      <data key="d4">Pau d'arco is an evergreen canopy tree native to the Amazon rainforest and other tropical regions of South and Central America that can grow over 30 meters high and 2-3 meters in diameter . Its wood is extremely dense and rot resistant . "Pau d'arco" is Portuguese for "bow tree", referring to the us</data>
      <data key="d5">⚠️ AVOID: Possibly Unsafe when used orally in typical doses. Animal studies have found that lapachol, a constituent of pau d'arco, has teratogenic and abortifacient effects ; avoid using. There is insufficient reliable information available about the safety of pau d'arco when used topically in pregnancy; avoid using.</data>
      <data key="d6" />
