      <data key="d3">https://naturalmedicines.therapeuticresearch.com/Data/ProMonographs/Pectin</data>
      <data key="d4">Pectin is a soluble fiber (polysaccharide) in fruits. It is a starch that is resistant to amylase. It is found in the cell walls of plant tissue and helps give plants rigidity . Pectin was used for years in combination with kaolin (Kaopectate). However, in April 2003, the FDA found insufficient supp</data>
      <data key="d5">✅ SAFE: Likely Safe when used in amounts commonly found in foods. Pectin has Generally Recognized as Safe (GRAS) status in the US .</data>
