      <data key="d1">Paeonia anomala</data>
      <data key="d2">Bai Shao | Chi Shao | Chinese Peony | Common Peony | Coral Peony | Cortex Moutan | European Peony | Jiu Chao Bai Shao | Moutan | Mu Dan Pi</data>
      <data key="d3">https://naturalmedicines.therapeuticresearch.com/Data/ProMonographs/Peony</data>
      <data key="d4">Peony is a perennial herb . The roots of peony species have been used in traditional Chinese medicine (TCM) for many purposes, including as an antipyretic or for the induction of vomiting, menstruation, or miscarriage . A common TCM peony preparation, total glucosides of peony (TGP), consists of a w</data>
      <data key="d5">⚠️ AVOID: Possibly Unsafe when used orally. Preliminary research suggests that peony can cause uterine contractions . However, other preliminary research suggests a combination of peony and angelica with or without motherwort, banksias rose, and ligustica, might be safe . Until more is known, avoid use.</data>
