      <data key="d4">Peyote is a type of cactus found mainly in dry regions from central Mexico to Texas. Parts of the cactus crown are commonly used in rituals and as a hallucinogen . The United States Drug Enforcement Administration (DEA) lists peyote as a Schedule I controlled substance. However, this listing does no</data>
