      <data key="d3">https://naturalmedicines.therapeuticresearch.com/Data/ProMonographs/Pheasants-Eye</data>
      <data key="d4">Pheasant's eye is a plant native to temperate regions of Europe and Asia . It has a history of use as a cardiac stimulant, especially in the previous Soviet Union . However, it is considered a poisonous plant . Traditional and historical uses of pheasant's eye include cramps, edema, epilepsy, and ca</data>
