      <data key="d1" />
      <data key="d2">1-Amino-2-phenylethane | 2-Phenethylamine | 2-Phenylethylamine | Benzeneethanamine | Beta-phenethylamine | Beta-phenylethylamine | Fenetilamina (PEA) | PEA | Phénéthylamine (PEA) | Phenethylamine HCl</data>
      <data key="d3">https://naturalmedicines.therapeuticresearch.com/Data/ProMonographs/Phenethylamine-PEA</data>
      <data key="d4">Phenethylamine is a monoamine alkaloid found in plants , bacteria , fungi , and animals including humans , as well as some foods such as chocolate and eggs . In the body, phenethylamine is produced via the decarboxylation of the amino acid, L-phenylalanine . In the central nervous system, phenethyla</data>
      <data key="d5">⚠️ AVOID: Insufficient reliable information available; avoid using.</data>
