      <data key="d4">The pitcher plant is a North American bog plant. Its leaves form a cup-shaped "pitcher" that can lure, capture, and digest insects . The pitcher plant extract, Sarapin, is an FDA-approved grandfathered product, meaning that it entered the market in accordance with the 1906 Pure Food and Drug Act pri</data>
