      <data key="d4">The plum is a fruit commonly eaten as food. Although there are over 40 species, the most common commercial plums are Prunus domestica and Prunus salicina. Dried plums, also known as prunes, are made almost exclusively from Prunus domestica because of their sugar content. Prunus salicina is the most</data>
