      <data key="d4">Rehmannia is a perennial plant that grows up to 30 cm tall. It is primarily cultivated in China where it is used extensively as a component in herbal decoctions of traditional Chinese medicine (TCM). The root of rehmannia, known for its sticky properties, is used in either fresh, dried, or steamed f</data>
