      <data key="d2">Chinese Rhubarb | Da Huang | Garden Rhubarb | Himalayan Rhubarb | Indian Rhubarb | Medicinal Rhubarb | Radix et Rhizoma Rhei | Rewandchini | Rhapontic Rhubarb | Rhei</data>
      <data key="d3">https://naturalmedicines.therapeuticresearch.com/Data/ProMonographs/Rhubarb</data>
      <data key="d4">Rhubarb is a plant. Its root is used as a food flavoring and the stalk is commonly consumed as food. The stalk, root, and rhizome of rhubarb are sometimes used medicinally. Rhubarb rhizomes and roots are used in traditional Chinese medicine, sometimes as part of combination decoctions such as Da-Che</data>
