      <data key="d4">Ribose is a pentose sugar which naturally occurs as D-ribose . It is a component of deoxyribonucleic acid (DNA), ribonucleic acid (RNA), adenosine triphosphate (ATP), guanosine triphosphate (GTP), and flavins such as flavin adenine dinucleotide (FAD) and riboflavin . It is also a structural componen</data>
