    <node id="Rice Bran">
      <data key="d0">supplement</data>
      <data key="d1">Oryza sativa</data>
      <data key="d2">Brown Rice Bran | Cereal Fiber | Dietary Fiber | Fibre Alimentaire | Fibre Céréalière | Huile de Son de Riz | Rice Bran Oil | Ricebran Oil | Riz de Son | Salvado de Arroz</data>
      <data key="d3">https://naturalmedicines.therapeuticresearch.com/Data/ProMonographs/Rice-Bran</data>
      <data key="d4">Rice bran is obtained from the outer hull of the rice Oryza sativa. It has been traditionally used to boost immunity and as an antioxidant. Rice bran oil is a popular "healthy oil" in Japan, Asia, and India . CHILDREN: Possibly Safe when used orally and appropriately in infants. Rice bran 1-5 grams</data>
      <data key="d5">⚠️ AVOID: Likely Safe when used orally in amounts commonly found in foods. There is insufficient reliable information available about the safety of rice bran when used for medicinal purposes during pregnancy and lactation; avoid using.</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
