      <data key="d0">supplement</data>
      <data key="d1" />
      <data key="d2">Apothecary Rose | Cherokee Rose | Cherokee Rose Musquée | Chinese Rosehip | Cynorhodon | Cynorhodons | Cynosbatos | Damask Rose | Dog Rose | Dog Rose Hips</data>
      <data key="d3">https://naturalmedicines.therapeuticresearch.com/Data/ProMonographs/Rose-Hip</data>
      <data key="d4">There are approximately 100 Rosa species found across Europe, Asia, and North America . Rose hip, which can be obtained from various Rosa species, is the ripe, dried receptacle (hip) of the rose that contains the pseudo fruit and seed . Rose hip is used traditionally in medicine for various gastroin</data>
      <data key="d5">⚠️ AVOID: There is insufficient reliable information available about the safety of rose hip when used orally or topically in medicinal amounts; avoid using in amounts greater than those found in foods.</data>
