    <node id="Rosemary">
      <data key="d0">supplement</data>
      <data key="d1">Rosmarinus officinalis</data>
      <data key="d2">Alecrim | Compass Plant | Compass Weed | Encensier | Herbe Aux Couronnes | Old Man | Polar Plant | Romarin | Romarin Des Troubadours | Romero</data>
      <data key="d3">https://naturalmedicines.therapeuticresearch.com/Data/ProMonographs/Rosemary</data>
      <data key="d4">Rosemary is a perennial, evergreen shrub native to the Mediterranean region and grown worldwide . Traditionally, rosemary has been used orally for gastric disorders, as well as for cough, anxiety, depression, gout, headache, insomnia, and liver and gallbladder complaints. It has also been used topic</data>
      <data key="d5">⚠️ AVOID: Possibly Unsafe when used orally in medicinal amounts. Rosemary might have uterine and menstrual flow stimulant effects , and might increase metabolism of estradiol and estrone ; avoid using. There is insufficient reliable information available about the safety of rosemary when used topically during pregnancy.</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
