    <node id="Rue">
      <data key="d0">supplement</data>
      <data key="d1">Ruta graveolens</data>
      <data key="d2">Aruta | Arvada | Common Rue | Garden Rue | German Rue | Herbe à la Belle-Fille | Herbe de Grâce | Herbe de la Rue | Herbe de Repentance | Herb-of-Grace</data>
      <data key="d3">https://naturalmedicines.therapeuticresearch.com/Data/ProMonographs/Rue</data>
      <data key="d4">Rue is a perennial, evergreen shrub that grows up to 1 meter in height. It is native to southern Europe . It has traditionally been used medicinally for genitourinary disorders and as an antimicrobial, antispasmodic, and diuretic . Rue and its essential oil have been used as flavoring agents in food</data>
      <data key="d5">⚠️ AVOID: Likely Unsafe when used orally. Rue has uterine stimulant and abortifacient effects ; avoid using. Deaths have been reported in women who used rue as an abortifacient .</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Rupturewort">
