      <data key="d4">Rupturewort is a plant most often found in temperate and southern regions of Europe and Russia. It is used traditionally in Moroccan and Algerian medicine . Traditional uses include urinary, biliary, and respiratory tract disorders, wound healing, and as a purifying agent, diuretic, and spasmolytic.</data>
      <data key="d5">⚠️ AVOID: Insufficient reliable information available; avoid using.</data>
      <data key="d6" />
