      <data key="d4">The slippery elm is a broad-leafed, deciduous tree native to eastern Canada and the eastern and central United States . Its name refers to the slippery consistency the inner bark assumes when it is chewed or mixed with water. Avoid confusing whole bark with inner bark, as it is the inner bark of sli</data>
