      <data key="d4">Stevia is a bushy, perennial shrub native to northeast Paraguay, as well as Brazil and Argentina, that is now cultivated in various parts of the world . In Paraguay, stevia has traditionally been used as a sweetener and contraceptive . Extracts from the leaves are available as sweeteners in a number</data>
