      <data key="d4">Sulforaphane is a chemical made during the processing or chewing of cruciferous vegetables, especially broccoli and broccoli sprouts. Sulforaphane is produced when glucoraphanin, a constituent of cruciferous vegetables, interacts with myrosinase, an enzyme that occurs naturally in these plants and i</data>
