      <data key="d3">https://naturalmedicines.therapeuticresearch.com/Data/ProMonographs/Sweet-Sumac</data>
      <data key="d4">Sweet sumac is a deciduous, bushy shrub with yellow flowers and dark red berries. It is native to rocky regions of the Eastern United States. It previously belonged to the same genus as poison oak, poison ivy, and poison sumac, but the poisonous species are now considered to be in a distinct genus .</data>
