      <data key="d4">Tapioca is a common starch derived from the cassava plant. It is used as a thickening agent and as a source of starch in noodles, puddings, bread, and other food products .</data>
      <data key="d5">⚠️ AVOID: Likely Safe when used orally in the amounts commonly found in food . There is insufficient reliable information available about the safety of tapioca when used in larger amounts as medicine during pregnancy or lactation; avoid use.</data>
