      <data key="d3">https://naturalmedicines.therapeuticresearch.com/Data/ProMonographs/Tart-Cherry</data>
      <data key="d4">Tart cherry refers to the fruit of the Prunus avium tree. There are more than 270 varieties of tart cherry, but only a few are important commercially . The most popular tart cherry variety grown in the US is the Montmorency cherry. While up to 97% of tart cherries grown are used for cooking and baki</data>
      <data key="d5">⚠️ AVOID: Likely Safe when the fruit is consumed in typical food amounts. There is insufficient reliable information available about the safety of tart cherry fruit or stem when used in medicinal amounts; avoid using.</data>
