      <data key="d2">Acide Dihydroxysuccinique | Acide Tartrique | Acide tartrique | Ácido tartárico | Dihydroxysuccinic Acid</data>
      <data key="d3">https://naturalmedicines.therapeuticresearch.com/Data/ProMonographs/Tartaric-Acid</data>
      <data key="d4">Tartaric acid is a type of alpha hydroxy acid. Alpha hydroxy acids are natural acids found in foods, including, but not limited to, citrus fruits, sugarcane, sour milk, apples, and grapes . Tartaric acid is the main organic acid in grapes, raisins, and wine. It is also found in tamarind . Potassium</data>
      <data key="d5">⚠️ AVOID: Likely Safe when tartaric acid is used orally in the amounts commonly found in foods. There is insufficient reliable information available about the safety of tartaric acid when used as a supplement during pregnancy or lactation; avoid amounts greater than those found in foods.</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
