      <data key="d3">https://naturalmedicines.therapeuticresearch.com/Data/ProMonographs/Taurine</data>
      <data key="d4">Taurine is often referred to as a non-essential amino acid, but it is actually an amino sulfonic acid. It is present in normal diets, with the highest levels found in meat, seafood, and eggs . Taurine can also be synthesized through oxidation and decarboxylation of cysteine in the liver. Amounts sup</data>
      <data key="d5">⚠️ AVOID: Likely Safe when used in amounts found in foods. There is insufficient reliable information available about the safety of taurine when used in medicinal amounts during pregnancy and lactation; avoid using.</data>
