      <data key="d4">Terminalia chebula is a deciduous tree which grows throughout India, Burma, Sri Lanka, and Mauritius . The fruit of this tree, called Haritaki, is used extensively in Ayurvedic medicine, often in combination with Terminalia bellirica and Indian gooseberry .</data>
      <data key="d5">⚠️ AVOID: Possibly Unsafe when used orally. One source warns against using Terminalia bellirica and Terminalia chebula during pregnancy; however, the reason for this warning is not described . Until more is known, avoid use.</data>
