      <data key="d3">https://naturalmedicines.therapeuticresearch.com/Data/ProMonographs/Theacrine</data>
      <data key="d4">Theacrine is a purine alkaloid, structurally similar to caffeine, found in several species of tea and coffee as well as in the seeds of Herrania and Theobroma plant species. It was first isolated from Camellia sinensis leaves in 1937. Theacrine is the major purine alkaloid found in Camellia assamica</data>
