      <data key="d2">Teaflavina | Théaflavin | Theaflavin-3-3'-digallate | Theaflavin-3'-gallate | Theaflavin-3-gallate | Théaflavine | Theaflavins</data>
      <data key="d3">https://naturalmedicines.therapeuticresearch.com/Data/ProMonographs/Theaflavin</data>
      <data key="d4">Theaflavin, also referred to interchangeably as theaflavins, is produced when fresh tea leaves are fermented to produce black tea. Theaflavin includes a group of closely related reddish-yellow polyphenol pigments that are important to the color and flavor of black tea .</data>
