      <data key="d1" />
      <data key="d2">2-Amino-4- (ethylcarbamoyl) Butyric Acid | 5-N-ethylglutamine | Gamma-ethylamino-L-glutamic acid | Gamma-glutamylethylamide | Gamma-N-ethylglutamine | L-gamma-glutamylethylamide | L-Theanine | L-Théanine | N-Éthyl-L-Glutamine | Teanina</data>
      <data key="d3">https://naturalmedicines.therapeuticresearch.com/Data/ProMonographs/Theanine</data>
      <data key="d4">Theanine is a major nonprotein amino acid that is chemically similar to glutamic acid . It is found in tea and was first isolated from green tea in the 1940s . Theanine is also found in some mushrooms . L-theanine is the predominant isomer of theanine that is found naturally in tea. Most clinical re</data>
      <data key="d5">⚠️ AVOID: Insufficient reliable information available; avoid using.</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
