      <data key="d4">Threonine is an essential amino acid, meaning that it is not synthesized by the body and must be obtained from the diet. In the diet, threonine is found in the greatest amounts in animal protein sources . Although threonine exists in four different stereoisomers, only L-threonine is biologically act</data>
