    <node id="Tree Turmeric">
      <data key="d0">supplement</data>
      <data key="d1">Berberis aristata</data>
      <data key="d2">Bérbero Indio | Chitra | Citra | Cúrcuma de Árbol | Darhahed | Darhald | Daruhaldi | Daruharidra | Darurajani | Darvi</data>
      <data key="d3">https://naturalmedicines.therapeuticresearch.com/Data/ProMonographs/Tree-Turmeric</data>
      <data key="d4">Tree turmeric is a shrub that is found in northern India and Nepal. It contains high levels of the constituent berberine . Tree turmeric has been used widely in Ayurveda and traditional Chinese medicine . CHILDREN: Likely Unsafe when used orally in newborns. The berberine constituent of tree turmeri</data>
      <data key="d5">⚠️ AVOID: Likely Unsafe when used orally. The berberine constituent of tree turmeric is thought to cross the placenta and may cause harm to the fetus. Kernicterus has developed in newborn infants exposed to berberine .</data>
      <data key="d6" />
