      <data key="d4">Trichopus zeylanicus is a rare plant native to India. It is commonly called "arogyapacha," which literally means "a plant that gives health and vitality" or "healthy green" . The fruit has been used as a local food source. It has also been used as an aphrodisiac and adaptogen, and to improve stamina</data>
      <data key="d5">⚠️ AVOID: Insufficient reliable information available; avoid using.</data>
