      <data key="d2">Dietas Vegetariana | Flexitarian Diet | Fruitarianism Diet | Lacto-Vegetarian Diet | Ovo-Vegetarian Diet | Pescotarian Diet | Plant-Based Diet | Régime végétarien | Semi-vegetarian Diet | Vegan Diet</data>
      <data key="d3">https://naturalmedicines.therapeuticresearch.com/Data/ProMonographs/Vegetarian-Diet</data>
      <data key="d4">A vegetarian diet consists of a dietary pattern focused on consuming plant-based products and avoiding or minimizing the consumption of animal products. Major types of vegetarian diets are the lacto-ovo-vegetarian diet and the vegan diet. In lacto-ovo-vegetarianism, meats are avoided, while milk and</data>
      <data key="d5">✅ SAFE: Likely Safe when used appropriately. A position statement from the Academy of Nutrition and Dietetics indicates that a nutritionally adequate vegetarian diet is appropriate during pregnancy and lactation . Following a vegetarian diet when pregnant or lactating should not pose a risk to the child as long as nutritional needs are met. Nutrients of concern may include omega-3 fatty acids, iron, zinc, calcium, vitamin D, and vitamin B12 . Additionally, one small observational study has found that co</data>
