      <data key="d4">Vetiver is a perennial grass native to India and Sri Lanka. It also grows in the tropical regions of Asia, Africa, Oceania, and Central and South America. The volatile oil from the roots is used in the perfume industry and as a food flavoring similar to lemongrass and citronella .</data>
