    <node id="Vibration Therapy">
      <data key="d0">supplement</data>
      <data key="d1" />
      <data key="d2">Biomechanical Muscle Stimulation | Biomechanical Oscillation | Biomechanical Stimulation | Direct Vibration | Focal Muscle Vibration | Local Vibration Therapy | Low Frequency Sound Stimulation | Mechanostimulation | Physioacoustic Vibration | Rhythmic Sensory Stimulation</data>
      <data key="d3">https://naturalmedicines.therapeuticresearch.com/Data/ProMonographs/Vibration-Therapy</data>
      <data key="d4">Vibration therapy is the use of vibration to promote health and recovery. Some types of vibration therapy involve the application of mechanical vibration to all or part of the body. This vibration is delivered through a variety of massage tools and/or specialized equipment . Another type of vibratio</data>
      <data key="d5">✅ SAFE: There is insufficient reliable evidence about the safety of vibration therapy. However, there is no reason to expect safety issues from short-term use.</data>
