      <data key="d4">Vitamin O is a product that claims to be a liquid form of oxygen. However, pure oxygen exists in liquid form only at temperatures below -183 degrees C. Also, water, by weight, is about 88% oxygen . The US Federal Trade Commission (FTC) states that Vitamin O appears to be nothing more than saltwater</data>
