      <data key="d3">https://naturalmedicines.therapeuticresearch.com/Data/ProMonographs/Vitex-agnus-castus</data>
      <data key="d4">The vitex agnus-castus tree is a deciduous shrub native to the Mediterranean and Central Asia . It has a long history of traditional use in ancient Egypt, Greece, and Rome. It has been used for menstrual and menopausal abnormalities, and for reducing sexual desire, giving it the common name "chaste</data>
      <data key="d5">⚠️ AVOID: Possibly Unsafe when used orally. Theoretically, the hormonal effects of vitex agnus-castus might adversely affect pregnancy or lactation . Animal research shows that taking vitex agnus-castus fruit extract when planning to become pregnant or during pregnancy may increase the risk of infertility, low fetal body weight, abortion, and stillbirth ; avoid using.</data>
