      <data key="d4">Wood anemone is a flowering plant traditionally used in folk medicine . Traditional uses include headache, stomach pain, gout, leprosy, lethargy, eye inflammation, delayed menstruation, whooping cough, asthma, and for its potential antimicrobial, diuretic, and abortive properties .</data>
      <data key="d5">⚠️ AVOID: Likely Unsafe when the fresh plant is used orally or topically . There is insufficient reliable information available about the safety of the oral or topical use of the dried, cut plant during pregnancy and lactation; avoid using.</data>
