      <data key="d3">https://naturalmedicines.therapeuticresearch.com/Data/ProMonographs/Wormseed</data>
      <data key="d4">Wormseed is an herb. Historically, the flowers have been used for their anthelmintic activity. More recently the leaves and stems have also been used for this purpose . However, wormseed can be toxic even in the amounts used for traditional purposes, such as the treatment of parasitic infestations .</data>
