      <data key="d2">Bacterial Polysaccharide | Corn Sugar Gum | Goma Xantana | Gomme de Sucre de Maïs | Gomme de Xanthane | Gomme Xanthane | Polysaccharide Bactérien | Polysaccharide de Type Xanthane | Polysaccharide Xanthane | Xanthan</data>
      <data key="d3">https://naturalmedicines.therapeuticresearch.com/Data/ProMonographs/Xanthan-Gum</data>
      <data key="d4">Xanthan gum is a polysaccharide consisting of repeating units of glucose, mannose, and glucuronic acid. It is produced by fermenting glucose, sucrose, or lactose with the bacterium Xanthomonas campestris .</data>
