      <data key="d4">Xylitol is a sugar alcohol with 5 carbon atoms. It is made from the plant-based sugar called xylose . Since xylitol has a sweet taste and lower glycemic index than glucose, it is used as an artificial sweetener . In the US, products containing xylitol are permitted to be labelled with a health claim</data>
      <data key="d5">⚠️ AVOID: There insufficient reliable information available about the use of xylitol in medicinal amounts during pregnancy and lactation; avoid using.</data>
