      <data key="d2">Acedera | Amalvelas | Broad-Leaved Dock | Chukkah | Curled Dock | Curly Dock | Field Sorrel | Herbe à Cochons | Lengua de Vaca | Narrow Dock</data>
      <data key="d3">https://naturalmedicines.therapeuticresearch.com/Data/ProMonographs/Yellow-Dock</data>
      <data key="d4">Yellow dock is a common and noxious weed found mainly in Serbia, Korea, and China. It is used in traditional medicine for its purported antimicrobial, anti-inflammatory, and laxative effects.</data>
      <data key="d5">⚠️ AVOID: Possibly Unsafe when used orally; avoid using. Yellow dock contains anthraquinone glycosides; unstandardized laxatives are not desirable during pregnancy .</data>
