    <node id="Yoga">
      <data key="d0">supplement</data>
      <data key="d1" />
      <data key="d2">Asana | Ashtanga Yoga | Bhakti Yoga | Bikram Yoga | Circular Yoga | Coiled Yoga | Creative Yoga | Dru Yoga | Exercice de Yoga | Hatha Yoga</data>
      <data key="d3">https://naturalmedicines.therapeuticresearch.com/Data/ProMonographs/Yoga</data>
      <data key="d4">Yoga is a key part of traditional Ayurvedic medicine. Yoga uses several exercises involving controlled breathing, meditation, and body posturing. Many different styles of yoga exist that use a variety of techniques at a range of intensities. Western yoga practice most often focuses on physical yoga</data>
      <data key="d5">✅ SAFE: Possibly Safe when used appropriately. Some clinical research shows that yoga during pregnancy does not adversely affect birth outcomes . However, some aggressive forms of yoga exercises might not be safe to use during pregnancy.</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
