      <data key="d2">Acidophilus Milk | Bulgarian Yogurt | Cultured Milk | Lait Acidophilus | Lait de Culture | Live Culture Yogurt | Probiotic | Probiotique | Yaourt | Yaourt Bulgare</data>
      <data key="d3">https://naturalmedicines.therapeuticresearch.com/Data/ProMonographs/Yogurt</data>
      <data key="d4">Yogurt is a dairy preparation produced by fermenting milk using one or more species of bacteria . In the United States, most yogurt is made via bacterial fermentation with Lactobacillus delbrueckii subsp. bulgaricus and Streptococcus thermophilus .</data>
      <data key="d5">✅ SAFE: Likely Safe when consumed in amounts commonly found in foods.</data>
      <data key="d6" />
