    <node id="Yucca">
      <data key="d0">supplement</data>
      <data key="d1" />
      <data key="d2">Adam's Needle | Aloe Yucca | Arbre de Josué | Bear Grass | Dagger Plant | Joshua Tree | Mohave Yucca | Mojave Yucca | Our-Lord's-Candle | Soapweed</data>
      <data key="d3">https://naturalmedicines.therapeuticresearch.com/Data/ProMonographs/Yucca</data>
      <data key="d4">Yucca is the common name for the more than 40 species of perennials in the Yucca genus. The plants are well known for their tough, sword-like leaves and a large spike of whitish flowers. They are native to the hot and dry parts of North America, Central America, and the West Indies, although they ar</data>
      <data key="d5">⚠️ AVOID: Insufficient reliable information available; avoid using.</data>
      <data key="d6" />
