    <node id="Zeaxanthin">
      <data key="d0">supplement</data>
      <data key="d1" />
      <data key="d2">(3R | 3'R)-Zeaxanthin | (3R | 3'S)-Zeaxanthin | (3R | 3'R)-Beta | beta-carotene-3 | 3'-diol | (3R | 3'S)-Beta</data>
      <data key="d3">https://naturalmedicines.therapeuticresearch.com/Data/ProMonographs/Zeaxanthin</data>
      <data key="d4">Zeaxanthin is a xanthophyll carotenoid. It is found along with its isomer lutein in the human macula and retina . Zeaxanthin consists of three stereoisomers, zeaxanthin itself (3R,3'R), meso-zeaxanthin (3R,3'S), and less commonly (3S, 3'S)-zeaxanthin . Zeaxanthin is found in high levels in foods suc</data>
      <data key="d5">✅ SAFE: Likely Safe when used orally and appropriately in amounts found in foods. Zeaxanthin is found in breast milk and levels correlate with infant status . Supplementation during pregnancy increases zeaxanthin levels in cord blood and infant skin . There is insufficient reliable information available about the safety of supplemental zeaxanthin.</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
