      <data key="d1">Curcuma zedoaria</data>
      <data key="d2">Cedoaria | Cetoal | Curcuma Sauvage | E Zhu | Essence de Zédoaire | E-Zhu | Gingembre Bâtard | Herbe à l'Estomac | Huile de Zédoaire | Indian Arrowroot</data>
      <data key="d3">https://naturalmedicines.therapeuticresearch.com/Data/ProMonographs/Zedoary</data>
      <data key="d4">Zedoary is a plant that grows to about 1.2 meters in height . It is native to northeast India, and cultivated widely in Asia . The rhizome is used medicinally. Traditional methods for preparing zedoary rhizome involve prolonged washing with water to remove most of the protein, water-soluble nutrient</data>
      <data key="d5">ℹ️ No pregnancy data available. Consult your physician.</data>
