    <node id="5-Deca Zol [Fast Facts]">
      <data key="d0">supplement</data>
      <data key="d1" />
      <data key="d2">5 deca zol | 5-deca zol - [DATOS BÁSICOS] | 5-déca zol - [FAITS EN BREF]</data>
      <data key="d3">https://naturalmedicines.therapeuticresearch.com/Data/ProMonographs/5-deca-zol-FAST-FACTS</data>
      <data key="d4">5-deca zol meets the definition of an anabolic androgenic steroid, as determined by the United States Designer Anabolic Steroid Control Act (DASCA) . It is unlawful for anabolic steroids to be added to dietary supplements. Anabolic steroids are also prohibited by the World Anti-Doping Agency (WADA)</data>
      <data key="d5">ℹ️ No pregnancy data available. Consult your physician.</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="5-Htp">
      <data key="d0">supplement</data>
      <data key="d1" />
      <data key="d2">5 Hydroxy-Tryptophan | 5 Hydroxy-Tryptophane | 5-Hydroxy L-Tryptophan | 5-Hydroxy L-Tryptophane | 5-Hydroxy Tryptophan | 5-Hydroxytryptophan | 5-Hydroxytryptophane | 5-L-Hydroxytryptophan | L-5 HTP | L-5-Hydroxytryptophan</data>
      <data key="d3">https://naturalmedicines.therapeuticresearch.com/Data/ProMonographs/5-HTP</data>
      <data key="d4">5-Hydroxytryptophan (5-HTP) is produced in the body from the essential amino acid L-tryptophan. It is converted to the neurotransmitter serotonin (5-hydroxytryptamine, 5-HT) . The 5-HTP found in supplements is often obtained commercially from the seeds of a tropical shrub, Griffonia simplicifolia .</data>
      <data key="d5">⚠️ AVOID: Insufficient reliable information available; avoid using.</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="To Cause Urticaria">
      <data key="d0">side_effect</data>
    </node>
    <node id="To Cause Gastrointestinal Side Effects Such As Nausea">
      <data key="d0">side_effect</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Abdominal Or Epigastric Pain">
      <data key="d0">side_effect</data>
    </node>
    <node id="6-Bromo [Fast Facts]">
      <data key="d0">supplement</data>
      <data key="d1" />
      <data key="d2">6 Bromo | 6-Bromo - [DATOS BÁSICOS] | 6-Bromo - [FAITS EN BREF] | 6-Bromoandrostenedione | 6-Bromo-Androstenedione | 6-Bronmandrostened ione</data>
      <data key="d3">https://naturalmedicines.therapeuticresearch.com/Data/ProMonographs/6-Bromo-FAST-FACTS</data>
      <data key="d4">6-Bromo is a steroidal aromatase inhibitor. An aromatase inhibitor increases levels of testosterone by inhibiting the conversion of testosterone to estrogen. It is marketed for concomitant use with anabolic steroids to reduce adverse effects (e.g. gynecomastia) from excess testosterone being convert</data>
      <data key="d5">⚠️ AVOID: Possibly Unsafe when used orally or parenterally. The U.S. Food and Drug Administration and other regulatory agencies warn that dietary supplements containing aromatase inhibitors are dangerous . Avoid using.</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="7,8-Benzoflavone [Fast Facts]">
      <data key="d0">supplement</data>
      <data key="d1" />
      <data key="d2">7 | 8-Benzoflavone | 7 | 8-benzoflavone - [DATOS BÁSICOS] | 7 | 8-benzoflavone - [FAITS EN BREF] | 7 | 8-BF | Alpha-Naphthoflavone | Alpha-Naphthylflavone</data>
      <data key="d3">https://naturalmedicines.therapeuticresearch.com/Data/ProMonographs/78benzoflavone-FAST-FACTS</data>
      <data key="d4">7,8-benzoflavone is a steroidal aromatase inhibitor. An aromatase inhibitor increases levels of testosterone by inhibiting the conversion of testosterone to estrogen. It is marketed for concomitant use with anabolic steroids to reduce adverse effects (e.g. gynecomastia) from excess testosterone bein</data>
      <data key="d5">⚠️ AVOID: Possibly Unsafe when used orally or parenterally. The U.S. Food and Drug Administration and other regulatory agencies warn that dietary supplements containing aromatase inhibitors are dangerous . Avoid using.</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="7-Alpha-Hydroxy-Dhea">
      <data key="d0">supplement</data>
      <data key="d1" />
      <data key="d2">7a-Hydroxy-Dehydroepiandrosterone | 7-Alfa-Hidroxi-DHEA | 7-Alpha-Hydroxy-Dehydroepiandrosterone | 7-Alpha-OH-DHEA | 7-Hydroxy DHEA | 7-Hydroxy-Dehydroepiandrosterone | 7-OH-DHEA</data>
      <data key="d3">https://naturalmedicines.therapeuticresearch.com/Data/ProMonographs/7-alpha-hydroxy-DHEA</data>
      <data key="d4">7-alpha-hydroxy-DHEA is a metabolite of dehydroepiandrosterone (DHEA) that occurs naturally in the body . 7-alpha-hydroxy-DHEA is considered a prohibited substance by the World Anti-Doping Agency (WADA) .</data>
      <data key="d5">⚠️ AVOID: Insufficient reliable information available; avoid using.</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="7-Beta-Hydroxy-Dhea [Fast Facts]">
      <data key="d0">supplement</data>
      <data key="d1" />
      <data key="d2">3b | 7b-dihydroxy-5-androsten-17-one | 7-beta-hidroxi-DHEA [DATOS BÁSICOS] | 7-bêta-hydroxy-DHEA - [FAITS EN BREF] | 7-Beta-OH-DHEA | 7b-Hydroxydehydroepiandrosterone | 7b-hydroxy-DHEA</data>
      <data key="d3">https://naturalmedicines.therapeuticresearch.com/Data/ProMonographs/7-beta-hydroxy-DHEA-FAST-FACTS</data>
      <data key="d4">7-beta-hydroxy-DHEA meets the definition of an anabolic androgenic steroid, as determined by the United States Designer Anabolic Steroid Control Act (DASCA) . It is unlawful for anabolic steroids to be added to dietary supplements. Anabolic steroids are also prohibited by the World Anti-Doping Agenc</data>
      <data key="d5">ℹ️ No pregnancy data available. Consult your physician.</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="7-Keto-Dhea">
      <data key="d0">supplement</data>
      <data key="d1" />
      <data key="d2">(3-beta)-3-hydroxyandrost-5-ene-7 | 17-dione | (3S | 8R | 9S | 10R | 13R | 14S)-3-hydroxy-10 | 13-dimethyl-2 | 3</data>
      <data key="d3">https://naturalmedicines.therapeuticresearch.com/Data/ProMonographs/7-Keto-DHEA</data>
      <data key="d4">7-keto-DHEA is a metabolite of the adrenal steroid, dehydroepiandrosterone (DHEA), which is formed in the body. Unlike DHEA, it is not converted to androgens or estrogens in the body and does not activate androgen or estrogen receptors .</data>
      <data key="d5">⚠️ AVOID: Insufficient reliable information available; avoid using.</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="7-Methoxyflavone">
      <data key="d0">supplement</data>
      <data key="d1" />
      <data key="d2">4H-1-benzopyran-4-one (synonyms: 7-methoxy-2-phenyl | 7-MF) | 7-Méthoxyflavone | 7-Metoxiflavona</data>
      <data key="d3">https://naturalmedicines.therapeuticresearch.com/Data/ProMonographs/7-Methoxyflavone</data>
      <data key="d4">7-methoxyflavone is a methylated flavonoid that can be chemically synthesized but has also been isolated from extracts of Zornia brasiliensis and from plants in families including Meliaceae and Rutaceae plants . Athletes are interested in 7-methoxyflavone for bodybuilding due to its proposed effect</data>
      <data key="d5">ℹ️ No pregnancy data available. Consult your physician.</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
