    <edge source="Phosphate Salts" target="Calcium">
      <data key="d7">INTERACTS_WITH</data>
      <data key="d8">0.9</data>
      <data key="d9">CALCIUM: Phosphates can cause a false decrease in serum and urine test results by inhibiting emission in some flame methods and by competing with EDTA for calcium .</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Phosphate Salts" target="Iron">
      <data key="d7">INTERACTS_WITH</data>
      <data key="d8">0.9</data>
      <data key="d9">IRON: Taking phosphate with iron can reduce the absorption of both iron and phosphate. Iron and phosphate interact in the gut to form insoluble precipitates. This effect seems to be increased in the p</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Phosphate Salts" target="Magnesium">
      <data key="d7">INTERACTS_WITH</data>
      <data key="d8">0.9</data>
      <data key="d9">MAGNESIUM: Taking phosphate with magnesium can reduce the absorption of both magnesium and phosphate. Magnesium binds phosphate in the gut . Magnesium salts, usually in combination with aluminum or ca</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Phosphate Salts" target="Hypercalcemia">
      <data key="d7">INTERACTS_WITH</data>
      <data key="d8">0.9</data>
      <data key="d9">HYPERCALCEMIA: Use cautiously in individuals with high serum calcium levels. The product of serum phosphate and calcium levels should not exceed 60 to prevent precipitation of calcium phosphate and so</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Phosphate Salts" target="Hyperphosphatemia">
      <data key="d7">INTERACTS_WITH</data>
      <data key="d8">0.9</data>
      <data key="d9">HYPERPHOSPHATEMIA: People with Addison disease or severe cardiopulmonary, kidney, or liver disease are at risk for hyperphosphatemia and hypocalcemia when taking phosphates . Hyperphosphatemia might a</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Phosphate Salts" target="Kidney Dysfunction">
      <data key="d7">INTERACTS_WITH</data>
      <data key="d8">0.9</data>
      <data key="d9">KIDNEY DYSFUNCTION: Closely monitor serum electrolytes when phosphates are used by people with mild to moderate kidney impairment .</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Phosphate Salts" target="Acid Phosphatase">
      <data key="d7">INTERACTS_WITH</data>
      <data key="d8">0.9</data>
      <data key="d9">ACID PHOSPHATASE: Phosphates can cause a false decrease in serum test results. High substrate concentrations can inhibit the analytic reaction .</data>
