    <edge source="Vitamin D" target="Calcium">
      <data key="d7">INTERACTS_WITH</data>
      <data key="d8">0.9</data>
      <data key="d9">CALCIUM: Vitamin D may increase the absorption of calcium in some people. Taking vitamin D along with calcium increases active absorption of calcium in the small intestine . One clinical study shows t</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Vitamin D" target="Magnesium">
      <data key="d7">INTERACTS_WITH</data>
      <data key="d8">0.9</data>
      <data key="d9">MAGNESIUM: Theoretically, vitamin D might increase the absorption of magnesium. The protein that transports calcium across the intestinal wall can also bind and transport magnesium. This protein is st</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Vitamin D" target="Arteriosclerosis">
      <data key="d7">INTERACTS_WITH</data>
      <data key="d8">0.9</data>
      <data key="d9">ARTERIOSCLEROSIS: High doses of vitamin D can cause hypercalcemia, which can contribute to arteriosclerosis, particularly in patients with kidney disease. Use supplemental vitamin D cautiously .</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Vitamin D" target="Histoplasmosis">
      <data key="d7">INTERACTS_WITH</data>
      <data key="d8">0.9</data>
      <data key="d9">HISTOPLASMOSIS: Vitamin D may increase calcium levels in people with histoplasmosis. In people with this condition, the metabolism of vitamin D to calcitriol is increased, which may increase the risk </data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Vitamin D" target="Hypercalcemia">
      <data key="d7">INTERACTS_WITH</data>
      <data key="d8">0.9</data>
      <data key="d9">HYPERCALCEMIA: Vitamin D supplements may precipitate and worsen hypercalcemia .</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Vitamin D" target="Hyperparathyroidism">
      <data key="d7">INTERACTS_WITH</data>
      <data key="d8">0.9</data>
      <data key="d9">HYPERPARATHYROIDISM: Vitamin D may increase calcium levels and lead to hypercalcemia in people with hyperparathyroidism. Use supplemental vitamin D cautiously .</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Vitamin D" target="Kidney Disease">
      <data key="d7">INTERACTS_WITH</data>
      <data key="d8">0.9</data>
      <data key="d9">KIDNEY DISEASE: Vitamin D may increase calcium levels and increase the risk of arteriosclerosis in people with kidney failure. This must be balanced with the need to prevent renal osteodystrophy. Moni</data>
    </edge>
