    <edge source="Gamma Butyrolactone (Gbl)" target="Bradycardia">
      <data key="d7">INTERACTS_WITH</data>
      <data key="d8">0.9</data>
      <data key="d9">BRADYCARDIA: Theoretically, use of GBL might cause additive bradycardia. GBL is metabolized to gamma-hydroxybutyrate (GHB), which can cause bradycardia ; avoid using.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Gamma Butyrolactone (Gbl)" target="Epilepsy">
      <data key="d7">INTERACTS_WITH</data>
      <data key="d8">0.9</data>
      <data key="d9">EPILEPSY: Theoretically, use of GBL might lower the seizure threshold. GBL is metabolized to gamma-hydroxybutyrate (GHB), which can induce seizures ; avoid using.</data>
    </edge>
