    <edge source="Scopolia" target="Anticholinergic Herbs">
      <data key="d7">INTERACTS_WITH</data>
      <data key="d8">0.9</data>
      <data key="d9">ANTICHOLINERGIC HERBS: Scopolia can potentiate the effects and adverse effects of other herbs with anticholinergic activity. Anticholinergic herbs include angels trumpet, belladonna, deadly nightshade</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Scopolia" target="Congestive Heart Failure (Chf)">
      <data key="d7">INTERACTS_WITH</data>
      <data key="d8">0.9</data>
      <data key="d9">CONGESTIVE HEART FAILURE (CHF): Contraindicated; scopolia might cause tachycardia and exacerbate CHF due to its hyoscyamine (atropine) and scopolamine content .</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Scopolia" target="Constipation">
      <data key="d7">INTERACTS_WITH</data>
      <data key="d8">0.9</data>
      <data key="d9">CONSTIPATION: Contraindicated; scopolia might cause constipation due to its hyoscyamine (atropine) and scopolamine content .</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Scopolia" target="Down Syndrome">
      <data key="d7">INTERACTS_WITH</data>
      <data key="d8">0.9</data>
      <data key="d9">DOWN SYNDROME: Caution, patients with Down syndrome might be hypersensitive to the antimuscarinic effects (mydriasis, positive chronotropic heart effects, etc.) of hyoscyamine (atropine) and scopolami</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Scopolia" target="Esophageal Reflux">
      <data key="d7">INTERACTS_WITH</data>
      <data key="d8">0.9</data>
      <data key="d9">ESOPHAGEAL REFLUX: Contraindicated; scopolia might delay gastric emptying and decrease lower esophageal pressure, promoting gastric retention and exacerbating reflux due to its hyoscyamine (atropine) </data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Scopolia" target="Fever">
      <data key="d7">INTERACTS_WITH</data>
      <data key="d8">0.9</data>
      <data key="d9">FEVER: Contraindicated; scopolia might increase the risk of hyperthermia in patients with fever due to its hyoscyamine (atropine) and scopolamine content .</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Scopolia" target="Gastric Ulcer">
      <data key="d7">INTERACTS_WITH</data>
      <data key="d8">0.9</data>
      <data key="d9">GASTRIC ULCER: Contraindicated; scopolia might delay gastric emptying and exacerbate gastric ulcers due to its hyoscyamine (atropine) and scopolamine content .</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Scopolia" target="Gi Infections">
      <data key="d7">INTERACTS_WITH</data>
      <data key="d8">0.9</data>
      <data key="d9">GI INFECTIONS: Contraindicated; scopolia might suppress GI motility causing retention of infecting organisms or toxins due to its hyoscyamine (atropine) and scopolamine content .</data>
    </edge>
